,"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TiredRebel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TiredRebel/job-hunt/commits/0f0b5da81463f965efc6a2aeafcdb8b5a4a4d02f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T10:05:48Z","email":"dlsaus@gmail.com","name":"TiredRebel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T10:05:48Z","email":"dlsaus@gmail.com","name":"TiredRebel"},"message":"perf(board): pointer-first collision detection, bounded drag re-renders\n\nclosestCenter picked drop targets by center distance, misfiring near\ncolumn boundaries; drag also re-rendered every mounted card on any\nboard state change. Adds boardCollisionDetection (pointerWithin ->\nrectIntersection fallback, closestCenter preserved for keyboard) so\ndrops resolve to what''s under the pointer, and memoizes the render\npath (StageCard, useQueries combine, stable callbacks).\n\nFound along the way: dnd-kit''s DndContext broadcasts active/over via\none shared React Context to every card, so a drag-start''s re-render\ncount on other-column cards has an architectural floor React.memo\ncan''t remove. Speed criterion redefined around render cost/regression\nbounds rather than zero re-renders (see design.md D2 addendum in the\narchived change). Also fixes a real bug found in the process:\nhandleDeleteJob/handleDragEnd depended on whole useMutation() result\nobjects, which react-query recreates every render, silently\ndefeating useCallback/memo downstream.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"764acb307e707434ca38ce6488caaa265816f4a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TiredRebel/job-hunt/git/trees/764acb307e707434ca38ce6488caaa265816f4a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TiredRebel/job-hunt/git/commits/0f0b5da81463f965efc6a2aeafcdb8b5a4a4d02f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_