/api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/49af2cbfa90778d6ce706af0c7a11e35acfb2c26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:57:49Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:57:49Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"feat(host-harness): load a panel remote the way Signal K Admin does\n\nThe new signalk-nearlcrews-ui/host-harness entry stands in for the Admin\nloader in consumer browser tests: createHostShareScope builds the Admin''s\nfallback share scope, loadPanelRemote routes on the script type the server\nwrites, and HostPanelFrame renders the panel inside the Admin''s Suspense and\nerror boundary with configuration state seeded from its prop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3620cddd76f6bc4a5411601e139a837dba5663b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/trees/c3620cddd76f6bc4a5411601e139a837dba5663b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/commits/49af2cbfa90778d6ce706af0c7a11e35acfb2c26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commit/49af2cbfa90778d6ce706af0c7a11e35acfb2c26","node_id":"C_kwDOTZnxtNoAKDQ5YWYyY2JmYTkwNzc4ZDZjZTcwNmFmMGM3YTExZTM1YWNmYjJjMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commit/e4622ab8dde9978cea519e16719d6102b11fd996","sha":"e4622ab8dde9978cea519e16719d6102b11fd996","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/e4622ab8dde9978cea519e16719d6102b11fd996"}],"sha":"49af2cbfa90778d6ce706af0c7a11e35acfb2c26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/49af2cbfa90778d6ce706af0c7a11e35acfb2c26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/e4622ab8dde9978cea519e16719d6102b11fd996/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:57:49Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:57:49Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"feat!: rename or remove six props, rework announcements, and repaint the themes\n\nProps and bundle keys:\n- LiveRegion.announceOnMount becomes deferFirstMessage, with the meaning\n  its name states.\n- ThemeToggle.labels becomes choiceLabels, and the bundle key\n  themeToggle.choices becomes themeToggle.choiceLabels.\n- Card.labelledBy, PanelShell.errorLabels, and PanelShell.unsupportedLabels\n  are removed in favor of aria-labelledby, labels.panelError, and\n  labels.unsupportedBrowser.\n- PopoverWidth no longer takes a number.\n\nAnnouncements and headings:\n- Toasts speak once through host regions mounted before the first toast.\n- The panel announcer gives each message its own node, and it is heard\n  while a modal overlay is open.\n- An announcing Banner, StatusIndicator, or Metric holds polite content at\n  mount for one beat, and settleMs speaks a changing message once it rests.\n- Nested sections are not landmarks by default, an unnamed Code block is a\n  group, and sections, InlineConfirm, and the error fallback inside a dialog\n  head below the dialog title.\n\nAdded: FreshnessNote, useResetDrafts, PANEL_LABEL_DEFAULTS, SaveActionBar\noutcome and focus targets, FieldValidity.firstInvalid, NamedUnit, visible\ndisabled reasons, SegmentedControlOption.ariaDisabled and dataAttributes,\nSwitch description and error, Section.leading, Stack divided,\nMenu.triggerProps, the border-subtle, neutral-subtle, and focus-ring-width\ntokens, and locale grouping in formatCount.\n\nChanged: Section and CollapsibleSection share one surface, section titles\nsize by depth, tone glyphs take a shape per tone, outlines take the subtle\nborder, Night paints the browser chrome, every focus ring reads one width\ntoken that a contrast request raises, NumberField shows its message once an\nedit finishes, and every thrown error starts with the package name.\n\nFixed: raised contrast tokens under prefers-contrast, blank bundle entries,\ncontrast on selected rows, focus rings under forced colors, the virtualized\nDataGrid selection bar, the docked ActionBar scroll jump, the RTL collapsible\nchevron, Button as=\"a\", disabled checkbox labels, and RelativeAge reading a\nnew timestamp against an old clock.\n\nThe unit suite is split into one spec per component, and the declarations\nbaseline records the public type surface.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the renamed and removed props and bundle keys above, the\nannouncement, landmark, and heading changes, the NumberField message timing,\nthe resolveFreshness skew rule, the new default strings, the prefixed error\nmessages, and the new inner elements in the field error, Card footer, and\nCollapsibleSection header. docs/migration.md lists each step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6052a3ec4434dc227c37a931887eed196d51cf3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/trees/6052a3ec4434dc227c37a931887eed196d51cf3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/commits/e4622ab8dde9978cea519e16719d6102b11fd996","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/