--\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T15:58:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commit/2f501135a78614921f2cbd1a70cdcd7d29ad8a1a","node_id":"C_kwDOTZnxtNoAKDJmNTAxMTM1YTc4NjE0OTIxZjJjYmQxYTcwY2RjZDdkMjlhZDhhMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commit/0b3197c96e3b537a92569c948f4f5f3fd2d6b694","sha":"0b3197c96e3b537a92569c948f4f5f3fd2d6b694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/0b3197c96e3b537a92569c948f4f5f3fd2d6b694"}],"sha":"2f501135a78614921f2cbd1a70cdcd7d29ad8a1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/2f501135a78614921f2cbd1a70cdcd7d29ad8a1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/0b3197c96e3b537a92569c948f4f5f3fd2d6b694/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T18:52:08Z","email":"23341701+NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T18:52:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"release: prepare 0.10.1 (#24)\n\nInstalls tab styles with `Tabs` rather than with every panel.\n\n## What changed\n\n`TABS_STYLES` was joined into the root sheet `PanelRoot` installs on\nmount, so a panel that renders no tabs still carried the rules and no\nbundler could drop them. That is most panels. It is now a `StyleModule`\nregistered in the manifest, installed by `Tabs` through\n`useOptionalModuleStyles`, the same way the progress bar, radio group,\nand switch already worked.\n\nThis was an incomplete split rather than a rule being broken:\n`TABS_STYLES` was never registered as a per-component module, so the\ncomment in `styles/index.ts` about not reaching one from there was not\nbeing violated. The rules simply never moved when the others did.\n\n## Size\n\n| | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| Root sheet, installed by every panel | 2,456 raw bytes smaller, 291\ngzip |\n| `signalk-nearlcrews-ui` entry point | 30,989 to 30,698 gzip |\n| `signalk-nearlcrews-ui/composites` | 16,567 to 17,256 gzip |\n\nThe composites entry grows because bundling that entry whole now pulls\nthe tab styles in with `Tabs`. A panel that does not render tabs drops\nthem instead, which is the case the change exists for.\n\n## Why this is safe for panels that do render tabs\n\nThe rules are identical. No other stylesheet references a tab class, and\n`tabs.ts` references no class it does not own, so moving the module\nafter the root sheet in the cascade cannot change a computed style.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Declarations match the baseline apart from three version literals, so\nthis is a patch with no public API change. `TABS_STYLES` is not exported\nfrom any entry point.\n- The manifest test that keeps per-component rules out of the root sheet\nnow covers tabs, and was verified to fail when the rules are put back.\n- `npm run validate` green: 1088 unit tests, no type errors, coverage\nfloors met, both Module Federation fixtures pass.\n- Browser suites green on all four projects: Chromium 64, Firefox 56,\nWebKit 58, and mobile Chromium 55.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags\n\nCo-authored-by: Nearl Crews <NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"12526183d400d202de02758ddecc5827e9022906","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/trees/12526183d400d202de02758ddecc5827e9022906"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/commits/0b3197c96e3b537a92569c948f4f5f3fd2d6b694","verification":{"payload":"tree 12526183d400d202de02758ddecc5827e9022906\nparent a6f892dab28889719c9b051b882d8c00c2dc25a3\nauthor Nearl Crews <23341701+NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com> 1789152728 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789152728 -0400\n\nrelease: prepare 0.10.1 (#24)\n\nInstalls tab styles with `Tabs` rather than with every panel.\n\n## What changed\n\n`TABS_STYLES` was joined into the root sheet `PanelRoot` installs on\nmount, so a panel that renders no tabs still carried the rules and no\nbundler could drop them. That is most panels. It is now a `StyleModule`\nregistered in the manifest, installed by `Tabs` through\n`useOptionalModuleStyles`, the same way the progress bar, radio group,\nand switch already worked.\n\nThis was an incomplete split rather than a rule being broken:\n`TABS_STYLES` was never registered as a per-component module, so the\ncomment in `styles/index.ts` about not reaching one from there was not\nbeing violated. The rules simply never moved when the others did.\n\n## Size\n\n| | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| Root sheet, installed by every panel | 2,456 raw bytes smaller, 291\ngzip |\n| `signalk-nearlcrews-ui` entry point | 30,989 to 30,698 gzip |\n| `signalk-nearlcrews-ui/composites` | 16,567 to 17,256 gzip |\n\nThe composites entry grows because bundling that entry whole now pulls\nthe tab styles in with `Tabs`. A panel that does not render tabs drops\nthem instead, which is the case the change exists for.\n\n## Why this is safe for panels that do render tabs\n\nThe rules are identical. No other stylesheet references a tab class, and\n`tabs.ts` references no class it does not own, so moving the module\nafter the root sheet in the cascade cannot change a computed style.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Declarations match the baseline apart from three version literals, so\nthis is a patch with no public API change. `TABS_STYLES` is not exported\nfrom any entry point.\n- The manifest test that keeps per-component rules out of the root sheet\nnow covers tabs, and was verified to fail when the rules are put back.\n- `npm run validate` green: 1088 unit tests, no type errors, coverage\nfloors met, both Module Federation fixtures pass.\n- Browser suites green on all four projects: Chromium 64, Firefox 56,\nWebKit 58, and mobile Chromium 55.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags\n\nCo-authored-by: Nearl Crews <NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpE3YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0MQQADeTLoI8DVy6MdzgAAng/q6Z\nlB0F1QM0bdZpG9WaR63aj7TxztF2L2Q/zj2YHOt9dkmq2VPqApqS8yev7KVG7CQa\nIADQJVvOybutpHgrkTx5K0ZO06Rq4vdjwDX8LnzLJ3ACn1wnHBBc/8BY+sXVZXKT\nLU3y4wBgMa5GXk+ovGGJqXBCSjQr69CWi+lDjJLND+/6DiI3KXCpWPBEvk7+Kcuo\nkyd7103nAzkvXmw37l/6sDTU7zXf4UB6Z9lxE5nUAIadtH2Te2OFo1r4+pZYZmTh\np/xE//7zEc+0ZU9ZX5rWo5ATkCSwmwzT0KercESamkRboBJsIHry5kZFl/xlqlny\nenBVctq0a+e9ffR0wuksY2Lu/TqaYg52uGOIDGm/jad6jdf7KBdnmC1rxS640O+h\nTMo+exSpL83S6EChWV7Fvc0VwuypkHEVVoHnKWuxm06eH4kCy+DV0K/kM/MIY8c+\nFua5eQ1WOJxff7dSdiclf2yv3eKC6+7PCQnEmynr8wt5bJf0Nf9rgqALnqoLpqnp\nUSAdcCmbFoqeaVpxXzoyNc1LPqx9U0z4ncdxcPSgz+rsXPP5jRzFFvJ1QC4cYWHz\n4SLSS+48HcZKF4M0/QMzghgk52gu7Gibb98kZ/SYcWfSOEfu+JmB2Cpy9lEmiBrz\nfmiC6VR0viM2ujBz+JUV\n=8IvY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T18:52:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commit/0b3197c96e3b537a92569c948f4f5f3fd2d6b694","node_id":"C_kwDOTZnxtNoAKDBiMzE5N2M5NmUzYjUzN2E5MjU2OWM5NDhmNGY1ZjNmZDJkNmI2OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commit/a6f892dab28889719c9b051b882d8c00c2dc25a3","sha":"a6f892dab28889719c9b051b882d8c00c2dc25a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/a6f892dab28889719c9b051b882d8c00c2dc25a3"}],"sha":"0b3197c96e3b537a92569c948f4f5f3fd2d6b694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/0b3197c96e3b537a92569c948f4f5f3fd2d6b694"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/a6f892dab28889719c9b051b882d8c00c2dc25a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:57:54Z","email":"23341701+NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:57:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"release: prepare 0.10.0 (#23)\n\nCloses the gaps six consumer panels hit in practice. Every change here\ncame from reviewing those panels against the shipped package rather than\nfrom inspecting the library on its own.\n\n## Live regions announce reliably\n\n`Banner`, `StatusIndicator`, and `Metric` with `live` set now mount the\nelement carrying the role before there is anything to say, so the\nconditional form that reads as obvious stops losing announcements. One\nconsumer had twelve call sites written that way and all twelve announced\nunreliably. `LiveRegion` takes `announceKey` to repeat an identical\nmessage.\n\n## Focus survives where it used to be destroyed\n\nA disclosure panel holding focus hands it to its trigger whoever closed\nit, a `Banner` does the same however it goes away rather than only on\nDismiss, and `Checkbox`, `CheckboxGroup` options, and `RadioGroup` can\nrefuse a change while staying focusable through `ariaDisabled` and\n`readOnly`. `InlineConfirm.busy` blocks Confirm alone, so Cancel and\nEscape keep working.\n\n## Headings nest\n\nSections inside a titled `PanelShell` take the level below the panel\ntitle instead of sitting beside it, so the outline a screen reader\nnavigates matches the one on screen. A `Banner` given a landmark role\nnames itself from its own visible title.\n\n## Styles ship per component\n\nA panel that renders a dialog and none of the in-flow controls drops\nabout 19 KB of stylesheet text, and the root sheet is 10,421 bytes\nsmaller. `Card density=\"flush\"` clears the row gap it used to leave\nbehind. No selector, declaration, or rendered result changed, verified\nby a computed-style comparison across 3,116 element snapshots.\n\n## Types and ergonomics\n\n`Tabs`, `Tab`, and `TabPanel` are generic over their value type, and\n`TabPanel` accepts a function child so `mountStrategy=\"unmount\"` means\ndo not build. `SaveActionBar` owns its saved-message window,\n`LabeledField` merges extra `aria-describedby` ids, `Disclosure` takes\n`id` and `idPrefix` and a `disclosure` prop on both parts, and\n`PANEL_CONTAINER_NAME` and `CONTAINER_BREAKPOINT_NARROW` are public.\n\n`snui-check-consumer` gains a `--runtime` mode that renders the built\nremote the way the Signal K Admin host does, so a consumer no longer\nmaintains its own list of the globals React Aria touches at import.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `validate`: all fifteen steps, including both Module Federation\nfixtures against the published share map\n- 1087 unit tests across 62 files, no type errors\n- Coverage 97.2 statements, 93.0 branches, 98.7 functions, 99.0 lines,\nagainst floors of 92, 85, 95, and 95\n- Browser: Chromium 64, Firefox 56, WebKit 58, and mobile Chromium 55,\nrun serially\n- `npm audit`: zero vulnerabilities\n- Packed tarball: 321 files\n\nThe hosted `ubuntu24-x64` and `ubuntu24-arm64` visual baselines do not\nneed regenerating.\n\n## Behavior to check\n\nNine behavior changes are written up in `docs/migration.md`, the notable\none being that sections inside a titled `PanelShell` now nest under it.\nNo current consumer is affected: five use a titleless shell and the\nsixth passes an explicit `headingLevel` at every call site.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad90f021cb6ad352cf1514a4c0e5d57196be3849","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/trees/ad90f021cb6ad352cf1514a4c0e5d57196be3849"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/commits/a6f892dab28889719c9b051b882d8c00c2dc25a3","verification":{"payload":"tree ad90f021cb6ad352cf1514a4c0e5d57196be3849\nparent e86a5e7b926d05b9ffa6a7664ae08bbec93254f3\nauthor Nearl Crews <23341701+NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com> 1789145874 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789145874 -0400\n\nrelease: prepare 0.10.0 (#23)\n\nCloses the gaps six consumer panels hit in practice. Every change here\ncame from reviewing those panels against the shipped package rather than\nfrom inspecting the library on its own.\n\n## Live regions announce reliably\n\n`Banner`, `StatusIndicator`, and `Metric` with `live` set now mount the\nelement carrying the role before there is anything to say, so the\nconditional form that reads as obvious stops losing announcements. One\nconsumer had twelve call sites written that way and all twelve announced\nunreliably. `LiveRegion` takes `announceKey` to repeat an identical\nmessage.\n\n## Focus survives where it used to be destroyed\n\nA disclosure panel holding focus hands it to its trigger whoever closed\nit, a `Banner` does the same however it goes away rather than only on\nDismiss, and `Checkbox`, `CheckboxGroup` options, and `RadioGroup` can\nrefuse a change while staying focusable through `ariaDisabled` and\n`readOnly`. `InlineConfirm.busy` blocks Confirm alone, so Cancel and\nEscape keep working.\n\n## Headings nest\n\nSections inside a titled `PanelShell` take the level below the panel\ntitle instead of sitting beside it, so the outline a screen reader\nnavigates matches the one on screen. A `Banner` given a landmark role\nnames itself from its own visible title.\n\n## Styles ship per component\n\nA panel that renders a dialog and none of the in-flow controls drops\nabout 19 KB of stylesheet text, and the root sheet is 10,421 bytes\nsmaller. `Card density=\"flush\"` clears the row gap it used to leave\nbehind. No selector, declaration, or rendered result changed, verified\nby a computed-style comparison across 3,116 element snapshots.\n\n## Types and ergonomics\n\n`Tabs`, `Tab`, and `TabPanel` are generic over their value type, and\n`TabPanel` accepts a function child so `mountStrategy=\"unmount\"` means\ndo not build. `SaveActionBar` owns its saved-message window,\n`LabeledField` merges extra `aria-describedby` ids, `Disclosure` takes\n`id` and `idPrefix` and a `disclosure` prop on both parts, and\n`PANEL_CONTAINER_NAME` and `CONTAINER_BREAKPOINT_NARROW` are public.\n\n`snui-check-consumer` gains a `--runtime` mode that renders the built\nremote the way the Signal K Admin host does, so a consumer no longer\nmaintains its own list of the globals React Aria touches at import.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `validate`: all fifteen steps, including both Module Federation\nfixtures against the published share map\n- 1087 unit tests across 62 files, no type errors\n- Coverage 97.2 statements, 93.0 branches, 98.7 functions, 99.0 lines,\nagainst floors of 92, 85, 95, and 95\n- Browser: Chromium 64, Firefox 56, WebKit 58, and mobile Chromium 55,\nrun serially\n- `npm audit`: zero vulnerabilities\n- Packed tarball: 321 files\n\nThe hosted `ubuntu24-x64` and `ubuntu24-arm64` visual baselines do not\nneed regenerating.\n\n## Behavior to check\n\nNine behavior changes are written up in `docs/migration.md`, the notable\none being that sections inside a titled `PanelShell` now nest under it.\nNo current consumer is affected: five use a titleless shell and the\nsixth passes an explicit `headingLevel` at every call site.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpDMSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/kkQAHQd+wuS8u1H8CvhXBtFG9in\nO+1ajSnuL5YNUF7Hy7Cvy8GD0iN87fnIqhhm0jDrwZnfPJQ9E71AfCQsrMh+SZI+\nCLZg2Rwg2sn3GTZbU7IlfDQ5OhEXmTwZBMHsRM8eGt85mNUkQjSXKcluk97BPEZc\ngNiheLC+V29VbqLx4sQ55kKxWi2cld6vuWwjB3yl7AkZ0gA/SB2+BXdu+ucqJVQn\n+vY0Q80tTxNoOoZAxK7P8Yqd7uONhkctD8sSqJTcY+r5QJ89eRI75CA8H20RCvw4\nVwR6wOIj8niS5ld18HvmuLGZPLNYClodZNPedG+TasOyciRE6abn45EE/HUME/UF\nIAt/zRq6COarwhBbgD0DfvwMzbkCONHlMozhadYDmAcX3NXiqsdivdjk/c/9qV5d\nf68m3JHKA0JXqqzpqm1vwdkPTmXqGqF4dqJrOYSP26N1hLqIUZGUC42wSstN