4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/commits/e86a5e7b926d05b9ffa6a7664ae08bbec93254f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:11:37Z","email":"23341701+NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:11:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"release: prepare 0.9.0 (#22)\n\nShips the panel scaffolding every consumer panel had rebuilt by hand, reworks\nthe Night palette and the token scales, delivers overlay and data-grid styles\nonly to the panels that use them, and publishes the Module Federation share\nmap with a consumer check command.\n\nA minor release with breaking changes; CHANGELOG.md and docs/migration.md\ncarry the full list.\n\nDefects this release would otherwise have shipped:\n\n- Switch, Radio, and SegmentedControl each throw at render without an\n  accessible name, and adding `label` beside the older prop had made both\n  optional, so the unnamed form compiled where 0.8.2 rejected it.\n- A toast raised while the panel sat outside the visual viewport was dropped\n  from the accessibility tree, so a failed save was never announced and could\n  not be reached.\n- A code block wider than the panel could not be scrolled by keyboard.\n- A Tabs whose selection matched nothing left the whole interface out of the\n  keyboard order.\n- Tapping a checkbox validation message to read it toggled the setting.\n- Clamp-mode number drafts committed values the input itself rejects, and a\n  step below 1e-6 rounded them to whole numbers.\n- Selectable data-grid rows and single-character segmented options sat under\n  the coarse-pointer target floor the rest of the library keeps.\n\nThirteen documented claims that contradicted the source are corrected, the\nREADME screenshots are generated by a script rather than by hand, and the\nbrowser suite now covers the components this release added, which is what\nfound the code-block failure.","tree":{"sha":"8202a4d3bb92e6d5b10008ea0e417f215cec3fe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/trees/8202a4d3bb92e6d5b10008ea0e417f215cec3fe4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nearlcrews-ui/git/commits/e86a5e7b926d05b9ffa6a7664ae08bbec93254f3","verification":{"payload":"tree 8202a4d3bb92e6d5b10008ea0e417f215cec3fe4\nparent d58202bcec8b2531bf1c5334eeceecca04ab89f3\nauthor Nearl Crews <23341701+NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com> 1788977497 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788977497 -0400\n\nrelease: prepare 0.9.0 (#22)\n\nShips the panel scaffolding every consumer panel had rebuilt by hand, reworks\nthe Night palette and the token scales, delivers overlay and data-grid styles\nonly to the panels that use them, and publishes the Module Federation share\nmap with a consumer check command.\n\nA minor release with breaking changes; CHANGELOG.md and docs/migration.md\ncarry the full list.\n\nDefects this release would otherwise have shipped:\n\n- Switch, Radio, and SegmentedControl each throw at render without an\n  accessible name, and adding `label` beside the older prop had made both\n  optional, so the unnamed form compiled where 0.8.2 rejected it.\n- A toast raised while the panel sat outside the visual viewport was dropped\n  from the accessibility tree, so a failed save was never announced and could\n  not be reached.\n- A code block wider than the panel could not be scrolled by keyboard.\n- A Tabs whose selection matched nothing left the whole interface out of the\n  keyboard order.\n- Tapping a checkbox validation message to read it toggled the setting.\n- Clamp-mode number drafts committed values the input itself rejects, and a\n  step below 1e-6 rounded them to whole numbers.\n- Selectable data-grid rows and single-character segmented options sat under\n  the coarse-pointer target floor the rest of the library keeps.\n\nThirteen documented claims that contradicted the source are corrected, the\nREADME screenshots are generated by a script rather than by hand, and the\nbrowser suite now covers the components this release added, which is what\nfound the code-block failure.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoaFZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU5QQAFeNKaraoOtS/J1g7B52h2vL\nZWNMNNSMheR/LA+NxwXVRPx1SehkjNYVXpWim+Fp/CS62H1TR3H0jjqMufaTqegX\ndIqLHkLC2GryT/Vf28bJdnvXoyR9E868f+rUAjZLitAc0R1j1Cd0EryVo4bxUMp3\nIrCmEoO+pc475c15QpZ6/Ql4pjY2L0rjoSnPhghEqGeAVVy4eDOXgzop13nyLkbj\nYu3Spv5d7ZauxnWJ0lGUIGyzzgvJjlAM0/1CP7c1FytQ7zRe8okM7DhAG2wCcWED\nBKhWGdm9DDrThyaCFlUQWEnCmssHeTiZ67cznUql6OU3h73idmGwXz4Z9mTm5iP2\nkOMVC3BKgyze6wg+1UUhFYWF6E2ro+sJCzmQFTbmqCXBuVNunJalqiJCYIRJacfp\nLqOgaVkDHOi8BmqT4DZSmho+ILlJjF3zVKrcnK+qgjMjLtqNTG1S4njz6TY7xgIz\nUcbwHEQ496fZCIcsh5yTm06eb49idfDHaTfOC9iSVAQFIldDPp9oeBjp0NOXOdpA\nCT5r9QNTHhlfFCEMZFDg0a+Io56vJh6dm0qTHbM79Z3vBWt3xCJF3lmfig5RAujt\nbGk/f2S50pssSdiFYe/M/uI8rEonsKdrbZF4263fvJjaYKQ/mlaze0vBVRxeQffu\n81k6GEVOwWfjB4Do6vks\n=Wrku\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T18:11:38Z"}},"committer":{"ava