.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"chore: trim repo guide, move glossary to docs/, prune local skills\n\n- CLAUDE.md cut to invariants + pointers; domain glossary now docs/GLOSSARY.md\n  (refs updated in README, ARCHITECTURE §6, code comments)\n- skills: single .claude/skills tree (.agents/skills symlink); removed\n  unused/duplicated skills (wizard, triage, aside-browser, research,\n  obsidian-vault, claude-handoff, git-guardrails, setup-pre-commit,\n  setup-ts-deep-modules, writing family, edit-article, docs-review,\n  review, thermo-nuclear-review); restored grilling/grill-me as shared\n  primitives; cleaned dangling refs in ask-matt/wayfinder\n- carries the earlier working-tree pass: comment purge, plan htmls\n  dropped (retrievable via git log -- plans/), dead fixtures removed","tree":{"sha":"d1aed7757294f8840ba138cfb7537e715d9f8ca6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/d1aed7757294f8840ba138cfb7537e715d9f8ca6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/efebd95bcfea3a3d57ac296eb0c93eacd261c3b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/efebd95bcfea3a3d57ac296eb0c93eacd261c3b3","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKGVmZWJkOTViY2ZlYTNhM2Q1N2FjMjk2ZWIwYzkzZWFjZDI2MWMzYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/4009adf9589012fa4bd96e0c4473d90f2f7fd4b5","sha":"4009adf9589012fa4bd96e0c4473d90f2f7fd4b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/4009adf9589012fa4bd96e0c4473d90f2f7fd4b5"}],"sha":"efebd95bcfea3a3d57ac296eb0c93eacd261c3b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/efebd95bcfea3a3d57ac296eb0c93eacd261c3b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/4009adf9589012fa4bd96e0c4473d90f2f7fd4b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:16:30Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:16:30Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"chore: apply two-axis review findings\n\nStandards and spec review of 7645a73 found no behaviour change and\nconfirmed the four security checks (safe_path_detail''s allowlist, the\nCodex reason/end_reason split, the build.rs/settings_commands/capabilities\nthree-way contract, and dedup_eq''s surviving invariants). These are the\nleftovers it did find.\n\n- ~25 more history comments purged: \"before this plan\", \"the old\n  contract\", \"the pre-fix code\", dangling `spec §N` citations across the\n  frontend, and a `Slice F` label.\n- ShortcutsSection''s prefix help text shipped \"(spec 171 §9)\" to the\n  settings window. Rewritten as plain English for a reader.\n- wire.rs gains five tests: safe_path_detail reads only file_path/path/\n  notebook_path, never forwards `command`, `description`, `prompt` or\n  any other key, and forwards a basename rather than a directory. The\n  helper had no test at all when it was three copies.\n- queue.rs, queue/tests.rs and queue/proptest_queue.rs get module headers.\n- capabilities/settings.json back to 2-space indent, matching default.json\n  and biome.json; contents unchanged.\n- plans/INDEX.md gains its line for this work.\n- docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md count updated for the five new tests.\n\ncargo test 964, vitest 748, clippy/fmt/tsc/biome clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcac59a826df9b871e4db4f55a06b58be1c435ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/dcac59a826df9b871e4db4f55a06b58be1c435ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/4009adf9589012fa4bd96e0c4473d90f2f7fd4b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/4009adf9589012fa4bd96e0c4473d90f2f7fd4b5","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKDQwMDlhZGY5NTg5MDEyZmE0YmQ5NmUwYzQ0NzNkOTBmMmY3ZmQ0YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/7645a7321382f872ecf5e1f77b3fe0b0ced8de7c","sha":"7645a7321382f872ecf5e1f77b3fe0b0ced8de7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/7645a7321382f872ecf5e1f77b3fe0b0ced8de7c"}],"sha":"4009adf9589012fa4bd96e0c4473d90f2f7fd4b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/4009adf9589012fa4bd96e0c4473d90f2f7fd4b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/7645a7321382f872ecf5e1f77b3fe0b0ced8de7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:05:20Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T18:05:20Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"chore: purge history from comments, finish telegram removal, split three modules\n\nComments across the rust core and the frontend described the product''s\npast: dates, deleted spec citations, plan and ticket numbers, review\ncredits, and \"what this used to be\" prose. CLAUDE.md''s writing rules say\ncomments describe the current product only. This makes that true.\n\n- ~1,550 comment lines removed across src-tauri/ and src/; invariants,\n  cross-file couplings and security boundaries kept and rewritten present\n  tense. Test names, test titles and assert messages cleaned too.\n- telegram: no code remained, only comments and one test naming it. The\n  test now covers the real guarantee (an unknown config table must not\n  fail Config::parse) without the name.\n- agents/providers: basename, safe_tool_name, safe_path_detail,\n  classify_notification, RawHookPayload and Mapped moved into wire.rs.\n  The safe_path_detail allowlist was written out three times and had\n  started to drift. Codex''s RawHookPayload uses `reason` where the others\n  use `end_reason`, so the shared struct carries both and each parser\n  still reads only its own field.\n- queue.rs: test modules relocated to queue/tests.rs and\n  queue/proptest_queue.rs. Production region byte-identical, nothing\n  widened to pub. 4,917 -> 1,304 lines.\n- lib.rs: tray menu and silence scheduling extracted to tray.rs with\n  their five tests. 3,460 -> 2,881 lines.\n- docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md test counts corrected to the real numbers.\n\ncargo test 959, vitest 748, clippy/fmt/tsc/biome all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"63384818f452ee0bfd5ac89b4c3443e76989241f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/63384818f452ee0bfd5ac89b4c3443e76989241f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/7645a7321382f872ecf5e1f77b3fe0b0ced8de7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/7645a7321382f872ecf5e1f77b3fe0b0ced8de7c","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKDc2NDVhNzMyMTM4MmY4NzJlY2Y1ZTFmNzdiM2ZlMGIwY2VkOGRlN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/0e9692b85b3e2dd98ec8a7a53ef8d6646c9cfaaa","sha":"0e9692b85b3e2dd98ec8a7a53ef8d6646c9cfaaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/0e9692b85b3e2dd98ec8a7a53ef8d6646c9cfaaa"}],"sha":"7645a7321382f872ecf5e1f77b3fe0b0ced8de7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/7645a7321382f872ecf5e1f77b3fe0b0ced8de7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/0e9692b85b3e2dd98ec8a7a53ef8d6646c9cfaaa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:58:44Z","email":"JAIN.CJ.CHETAN@gmail.com","name":"Chetan Jain"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:58:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"The Big Cleanup — anti-slop (chore/anti-slop-cleanup) (#20)\n\n* refactor(tokens): move --media-mint into app-only notchtap-tokens.css\n\nShared-ui tokens.css no longer carries the notchtap-specific media\naccent; both UI entries load src/notchtap-tokens.css right after the\nshared package, and entryImportOrder.test.ts enforces the order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(opencode): export { id, server } default shape for OpenCode 1.18\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: condense CLAUDE.md, add Figma design-system doc and unified reference\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: vendor anti-slop oxlint plugin and config (no code fixes yet)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): big-cleanup plan draft 3 — six audits consolidated\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): big-cleanup plan draft 4 — decisions locked\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: comment/doc convention — current product only, no history in prose\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: remove dead weight — unused assets, orphan files, dead deps/components\n\n- 9 unreferenced branding PNGs (kept used 128px mark + 1024px master)\n- unified.html orphan, superseded hooks/ shell hook, Windows .ico\n- @testing-library/jest-dom, unused npm scripts, dead Separator/CardAction/CardFooter\n- bundle.targets narrowed to app+dmg; shadcn kept (its tailwind.css is load-bearing)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): v5 corrections — verified counts, real enter/o gap, PR step\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): v6 — local reviewer agents gate before the PR\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: current-product-only rewrite — plans collapse to INDEX.md\n\n- 188 plan files + review logs + shipped specs removed (all in git history)\n- ARCHITECTURE absorbs the settings-command contract and agent adapter contract\n- TESTING_STRATEGY absorbs the manual checklist; weather/media content dropped\n- CLAUDE.md 137→86 lines, glossary slimmed, archaeology stripped\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat!: remove media/now-playing and weather verticals, secrets store, connector framework; tabs 5→3\n\n- now_playing.rs + vendored mediaremote-adapter (4.2MB) + media UI/CSS gone\n- weather_poller.rs + weather UI/art gone; SourceKind loses Weather\n- compat: stale config rotation_order with removed origins heals at boot (tested);\n  history entries with removed origins skipped, not fatal (tested)\n- secrets machinery + set_secret/get_secret_status removed; command allowlist 17→15\n  (settings_commands.rs + capabilities/settings.json + generate_handler in lockstep)\n- notifier.rs connector framework unthreaded from Engine/http\n- Tab enum 5→3 (agent/football/news); prefix digits 1–3; parity tests re-pinned\n- gates: cargo 959, vitest 746, tsc/biome/clippy/fmt clean; overlay capabilities untouched\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: remove reduced-motion support — app-wide non-goal\n\n+30/-275 across 19 files; MotionConfig wrapper gone from overlay entry;\nsettings MotionConfig keeps its load-bearing transition; 9 CSS @media blocks\ndeleted, no keyframes orphaned; ARCHITECTURE records the non-goal decision\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): v7 — test-trim workstream added\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: comment purge — web + agents/hover/poller retain only current-product notes\n\n* chore: comment purge wave 2 — remaining web components, css, lib, settings\n\n* chore: lint phase 0/1 — rule tuning, module-mocking override, adapter small fixes, symbol renames\n\n* chore: anti-slop wave 3 — guards/error, prototype trim, rust/web comment purge, oxlint gating, kharcha-inspired structure doc\n\n- src/lib/guards.ts + guards.test.ts (7 tests) and src/lib/error.ts: centralize\n  isString/isNumber/isFunction/isPositiveFiniteNumber/isNonNegativeInteger\n  and describeActionError; dedupe 3 Agent+Slot+Status copies; replace\n  typeof checks in 6 web files and presentationFacts; adapter resolvePort\n  now uses globalThis.process?.env\n- prototype/*.html: trim 5 headers to one-line static-mock lines (all 9 now 1 line)\n- src-tauri/src: line-local purge of plan history refs, 445 -> 53 refs\n  (small files 241->23, queue.rs 18, lib.rs 4); 30 web comment files purged;\n  cargo test --locked still 953 passed\n- justfile check-web and .github/workflows/ci.yml web job now run npx oxlint;\n  oxlint 0 errors, tsc clean, vitest 748, biome 2 expected CONTROL_CHARS errors\n- docs: add plans/2026-08-17-structure-kharcha-inspired.html (Kharcha lib/hooks\n  mapping to notchtap) and publish as postplan draft\n\nCo-Authored-By: internal-model\n\n* chore: structure — kharcha-inspired lib/hooks, board expand, prototype-safe tables\n\n- docs: CLAUDE.md add file-structure section (lib/constants, lib/format,\n  lib/guards, hooks/, components/ui, settings/sections, src-tauri/agents)\n  mirroring Kharcha lib/constants, lib/format, lib/validation, hooks/\n- src/lib/constants.ts + src/lib/format.ts: singletons for shared\n  constants and formatters (animationTiming re-export, byteFormat/timeFormat\n  re-exports); new code imports from lib/*\n- src/hooks/: move 8 hooks from src/ root (useAgentState, useSlotState,\n  useStatusState, useTabSelection, useAgentViewedSession, useDelayedSwap,\n  useClock, useExitChoreography) with re-exports at old paths for compat;\n  fix relative imports (./lib -> ../lib)\n- fix: AgentBoard expanded prop now respects keyboard expand flag, not hover-only\n- fix: HistorySection prototype-safe lookups via hasOwnProperty.call for PRIORITY_LABELS and SOURCE_ORIGIN_COLORS\n- fix: adapters/opencode BUS_EVENT_MAPPERS plain object -> Map, lookup via Map.get (prototype-safe) with SAFETY comment\n\nCo-Authored-By: internal-model\n\n* docs: update Big Cleanup estimate to 2026-08-17 — gates 953/748, 12.6k comments, structure, post-landing\n\n- draft 8 -> 9, dates 2026-08-17, Done means now lists 953/748, 445->53 Rust refs,\n  Kharcha-inspired lib/hooks structure, defects (board expand, prototype-safe),\n  369->0 lint, path alias @/* via tsconfig/vite, post-landing PR + Mini checklist\n- add plans/test-trim-audit.md: keep list, cut candidates (~80 tests), 30-45%\n  target, execution order; actual collapse after PR\n\nCo-Authored-By: internal-model\n\n* fix: gate regressions from the structure/comment-purge waves\n\n- Object.hasOwn (needs ES2022 lib) -> Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call\n  in HistorySection.tsx; tsconfig targets ES2020. Local tsc missed this\n  behind a stale .tsbuildinfo cache — would have failed CI on a fresh clone.\n- adapters/opencode/notchtap.ts: biome-ignore must be the comment directly\n  above the flagged line; the oxlint-disable line between it and the regex\n  broke that adjacency, so biome still flagged 2 control-char errors + an\n  unused-suppression warning. Reordered the two directive comments.\n- src/lib/guards.ts: isFunction predicate used the banned bare Function\n  type; narrowed to the safe (...args: never[]) => unknown top-type biome\n  itself suggests. Behavior-identical, call site''s existing cast untouched.\n- Biome import-order auto-fix in the new src/lib/ barrel files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve npm audit high-severity findings via safe transitive bumps\n\nnpm audit --audit-level=high was a known pre-existing gap (7 findings, all\ntransitive through shadcn''s toolchain deps) that would fail CI''s web job.\n''npm audit fix'' (no --force) resolved all 7 within existing semver ranges —\npackage.json untouched, only package-lock.json bumped. 0 vulnerabilities now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: clippy doc-comment formatting, rustfmt, and a suppression-adjacency conflict\n\n- 84 clippy::doc_lazy_continuation errors: 9 rust files had multi-line ///\n  bullet lists left unindented by the comment-purge pass; indented per\n  clippy''s own suggested fix, no prose content changed.\n- cargo fmt: pre-existing trailing-whitespace drift across 8 core files,\n  unrelated to this branch''s edits; mechanical cargo fmt, no semantic change.\n- adapters/opencode/notchtap.ts: biome-ignore and oxlint-disable-next-line\n  can''t both occupy ''the line directly before'' the same target — fixing one\n  broke the other. Moved oxlint''s suppression to a same-line\n  oxlint-disable-line trailing comment so both tools see their directive\n  adjacent to what it suppresses.\n- src/lib/guards.ts: isFunction''s (...args: never[]) => unknown return type\n  itself tripped anti-slop''s no-unknown-returns rule. void is the correct,\n  narrower top-type for a predicate whose return value is never used.\n\nGates green: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy -D warnings (0), cargo test\n(953), oxlint (0), biome ci (0), tsc --noEmit, vitest (748), vite build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: fix two comment artifacts found by security review\n\n- history.rs: dangling comma left by a plan-citation strip in two doc comments\n- build.rs + settings_commands.rs: stale ''eighteen''/''seventeen'' command\n  counts, left over from before the secrets-store removal dropped it to 15\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: clean up review-flagged leftovers from the weather/media removal\n\n- prototype/weather-art.html deleted (whole page for a removed feature,\n  violated CLAUDE.md''s ''mirrors shipped surfaces only'' rule); nav renumbered\n  in prototype/index.html, its stale hover-peek/status-dot descriptions\n  corrected against the real components.\n- prototype/status-rail.html: purged every weather/media CSS rule, JS demo\n  function, and demo frame (156 removed / 20 added); verified by extracting\n  and syntax-checking the <script> block and balancing style-block brackets.\n- prototype/control-panel.html: dropped the ''Now playing'' toggle doc block —\n  GeneralSection has no such toggle since media removal.\n- src/assets/weather/: 9 orphaned SVG glyphs + NOTICE deleted, zero remaining\n  importers.\n- src/App.test.tsx: dropped a stale weather key from a mocked status payload.\n- src-tauri/{settings,config,queue,tabs,event}.rs: repaired 5 comments left\n  grammatically broken by the plan-citation strip, two of which cited the\n  already-deleted notifier.rs.\n- src/overlay/source-identity.css: dropped a stale plan number and a\n  weather example from a comment describing a still-accurate CSS law.\n- src/settings/sections/HistorySection.tsx: two biome-ignore comments for\n  the Object.hasOwn-vs-ES2020-lib tension already fixed for tsc.\n\nGates green: cargo test (953), cargo fmt/clippy, vitest (748), tsc, biome\n(0 errors/warnings), oxlint (0), vite build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b6b9af6bbb32a3500fc8bd7c54dffcd10aa43e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/3b6b9af6bbb32a3500fc8bd7c54dffcd10aa43e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/0e9692b85b3e2dd98ec8a7a53ef8d6646c9cfaaa","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b6b9af6bbb32a3500fc8bd7c54dffcd10aa43e8\nparent 21590285543b94f216e8d1379d0195170d2e8088\nauthor Chetan Jain <JAIN.CJ.CHETAN@gmail.com> 1786892324 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786892324 +0530\n\nThe Big Cleanup — anti-slop (chore/anti-slop-cleanup) (#20)\n\n* refactor(tokens): move --media-mint into app-only notchtap-tokens.css\n\nShared-ui tokens.css no longer carries the notchtap-specific media\naccent; both UI entries load src/notchtap-tokens.css right after the\nshared package, and entryImportOrder.test.ts enforces the order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(opencode): export { id, server } default shape for OpenCode 1.18\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: condense CLAUDE.md, add Figma design-system doc and unified reference\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: vendor anti-slop oxlint plugin and config (no code fixes yet)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): big-cleanup plan draft 3 — six audits consolidated\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): big-cleanup plan draft 4 — decisions locked\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: comment/doc convention — current product only, no history in prose\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: remove dead weight — unused assets, orphan files, dead deps/components\n\n- 9 unreferenced branding PNGs (kept used 128px mark + 1024px master)\n- unified.html orphan, superseded hooks/ shell hook, Windows .ico\n- @testing-library/jest-dom, unused npm scripts, dead Separator/CardAction/CardFooter\n- bundle.targets narrowed to app+dmg; shadcn kept (its tailwind.css is load-bearing)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): v5 corrections — verified counts, real enter/o gap, PR step\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): v6 — local reviewer agents gate before the PR\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: current-product-only rewrite — plans collapse to INDEX.md\n\n- 188 plan files + review logs + shipped specs removed (all in git history)\n- ARCHITECTURE absorbs the settings-command contract and agent adapter contract\n- TESTING_STRATEGY absorbs the manual checklist; weather/media content dropped\n- CLAUDE.md 137→86 lines, glossary slimmed, archaeology stripped\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat!: remove media/now-playing and weather verticals, secrets store, connector framework; tabs 5→3\n\n- now_playing.rs + vendored mediaremote-adapter (4.2MB) + media UI/CSS gone\n- weather_poller.rs + weather UI/art gone; SourceKind loses Weather\n- compat: stale config rotation_order with removed origins heals at boot (tested);\n  history entries with removed origins skipped, not fatal (tested)\n- secrets machinery + set_secret/get_secret_status removed; command allowlist 17→15\n  (settings_commands.rs + capabilities/settings.json + generate_handler in lockstep)\n- notifier.rs connector framework unthreaded from Engine/http\n- Tab enum 5→3 (agent/football/news); prefix digits 1–3; parity tests re-pinned\n- gates: cargo 959, vitest 746, tsc/biome/clippy/fmt clean; overlay capabilities untouched\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: remove reduced-motion support — app-wide non-goal\n\n+30/-275 across 19 files; MotionConfig wrapper gone from overlay entry;\nsettings MotionConfig keeps its load-bearing transition; 9 CSS @media blocks\ndeleted, no keyframes orphaned; ARCHITECTURE records the non-goal decision\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(plans): v7 — test-trim workstream added\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: comment purge — web + agents/hover/poller retain only current-product notes\n\n* chore: comment purge wave 2 — remaining web components, css, lib, settings\n\n* chore: lint phase 0/1 — rule tuning, module-mocking override, adapter small fixes, symbol renames\n\n* chore: anti-slop wave 3 — guards/error, prototype trim, rust/web comment purge, oxlint gating, kharcha-inspired structure doc\n\n- src/lib/guards.ts + guards.test.ts (7 tests) and src/lib/error.ts: centralize\n  isString/isNumber/isFunction/isPositiveFiniteNumber/isNonNegativeInteger\n  and describeActionError; dedupe 3 Agent+Slot+Status copies; replace\n  typeof checks in 6 web files and presentationFacts; adapter resolvePort\n  now uses globalThis.process?.env\n- prototype/*.html: trim 5 headers to one-line static-mock lines (all 9 now 1 line)\n- src-tauri/src: line-local purge of plan history refs, 445 -> 53 refs\n  (small files 241->23, queue.rs 18, lib.rs 4); 30 web comment files purged;\n  cargo test --locked still 953 passed\n- justfile check-web and .github/workflows/ci.yml web job now run npx oxlint;\n  oxlint 0 errors, tsc clean, vitest 748, biome 2 expected CONTROL_CHARS errors\n- docs: add plans/2026-08-17-structure-kharcha-inspired.html (Kharcha lib/hooks\n  mapping to notchtap) and publish as postplan draft\n\nCo-Authored-By: internal-model\n\n* chore: structure — kharcha-inspired lib/hooks, board expand, prototype-safe tables\n\n- docs: CLAUDE.md add file-structure section (lib/constants, lib/format,\n  lib/guards, hooks/, components/ui, settings/sections, src-tauri/agents)\n  mirroring Kharcha lib/constants, lib/format, lib/validation, hooks/\n- src/lib/constants.ts + src/lib/format.ts: singletons for shared\n  constants and formatters (animationTiming re-export, byteFormat/timeFormat\n  re-exports); new code imports from lib/*\n- src/hooks/: move 8 hooks from src/ root (useAgentState, useSlotState,\n  useStatusState, useTabSelection, useAgentViewedSession, useDelayedSwap,\n  useClock, useExitChoreography) with re-exports at old paths for compat;\n  fix relative imports (./lib -> ../lib)\n- fix: AgentBoard expanded prop now respects keyboard expand flag, not hover-only\n- fix: HistorySection prototype-safe lookups via hasOwnProperty.call for PRIORITY_LABELS and SOURCE_ORIGIN_COLORS\n- fix: adapters/opencode BUS_EVENT_MAPPERS plain object -> Map, lookup via Map.get (prototype-safe) with SAFETY comment\n\nCo-Authored-By: internal-model\n\n* docs: update Big Cleanup estimate to 2026-08-17 — gates 953/748, 12.6k comments, structure, post-landing\n\n- draft 8 -> 9, dates 2026-08-17, Done means now lists 953/748, 445->53 Rust refs,\n  Kharcha-inspired lib/hooks structure, defects (board expand, prototy