9)\n\nThe operator rotated the exposed credential at the close of the PR #18\ncleanup review. Plan 065''s record still said \"accepted risk, no\nrotation performed\", which is now false and would send a future audit\nchasing a rotation that already happened.\n\nBoth halves of 065 are now satisfied: the working-tree copies went with\nthe AI-tooling cleanup, and rotation killed the string that stays in\nhistory. No history rewrite is needed — a dead key is not a credential.\n\nThe 2026-07-21 accepted-risk closure is kept in place as historical\nrecord and marked superseded rather than deleted, so the reasoning\ntrail stays readable.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcL/nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFX8QAEKIXwxrpX3UpLzvhJUcKoEp\nygsMtVtP0jnZB+F+Trx8CUuyqOH2uFKvun/rXOKZ6Lffd9WUBZnuyXR79UbAzUqC\nqEN0EEiYeHm7nBwoTb6Q2/75JMazjsCSiHtDy8anzThM/NtCcYcwQjYbaaHEHkM4\n+dwY+ITB1+TYYfvotpxNaZrKCU9VGajtyXeEde9HFAkfIcUMllS70bR12FX0YWGQ\nyh8hEq4Q45IQijL5kuBjfNa4c8L1+ydRoA1rNb1+FJoFf8Q2bDHp1UdWNtVbFHc2\n2cp6cOuHiQXlU/lsUutrrnM7Y5vi2F/QZf1J+m2Bd9ksDe2Y+KYEGoWiIkH1roF7\nTg/JNYUEXYgbvgf0/avCgdO7UTpc0sKyuFbzIGh1H5pTit1ROA4KnElNN4C1/hCt\nbPrXS0PlDbrKo672fyX7ztIhtEbfCwLNdVgk6Kp2C7h/gu6pAhOSfjnCtqFucgA1\njrWsQpgCfgO1jBCdpMQXSsGEyE+O86HI90blelHj+fqAedpKie4+M0T6f9mWwQeA\nCq+0PH8OBjG6mBSUAB+wSqHCmQVnOSXUA8RkeofM26xXaSSCVfISqk4B/EmVJxB0\nFe7o16d7+mnVEUyNWfIhotQsSBPI0vf9CA13nZVE5Tm0cV+BJ0sNtTWNEYPb4neY\n/2o2dHJBh6L9BIrosd5f\n=0NDE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T16:21:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/21590285543b94f216e8d1379d0195170d2e8088","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKDIxNTkwMjg1NTQzYjk0ZjIxNmU4ZDEzNzlkMDE5NTE3MGQyZTgwODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/f7475009466764d0eaf355fa8b661b10159e6665","sha":"f7475009466764d0eaf355fa8b661b10159e6665","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/f7475009466764d0eaf355fa8b661b10159e6665"}],"sha":"21590285543b94f216e8d1379d0195170d2e8088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/21590285543b94f216e8d1379d0195170d2e8088"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/f7475009466764d0eaf355fa8b661b10159e6665/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:05:40Z","email":"JAIN.CJ.CHETAN@gmail.com","name":"Chetan Jain"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:05:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: consolidate repository references and AI tooling (#18)\n\n* chore: consolidate repository references and AI tooling\n\n* docs: close the cleanup''s review findings\n\nSix fixes from the PR #18 review round (CodeRabbit x2, own pass x4):\n\n- .gitignore: the comment named a \"root `skills` symlink\" that does not\n  exist; the one tracked path is `.agents/skills` (CodeRabbit).\n- prototype/weather-art.html: the body lede still said the glyphs were\n  \"vendored locally\" after the page moved to loading them from\n  ../src/assets/weather/ (CodeRabbit).\n- the tab-notch spec still declared the two deleted mocks \"Design\n  sources of truth (binding)\", with a tie-break rule (\"the mock wins\"\n  on values) that nothing could honor once they were gone. Shipped\n  src/ is authoritative now; the mocks are recorded as historical\n  provenance, retrievable via git log and branch\n  feat/tab-notch-redesign.\n- plan 065''s closure had been quietly reopened: the cleanup addendum\n  read as \"rotation is still required\", contradicting the operator''s\n  recorded accepted-risk decision and dropping its do-not-re-file\n  guard. Restored in both plans/README.md and the plan file, with the\n  working-tree removal recorded as a side effect that changes nothing\n  about the acceptance.\n- CLAUDE.md: added a record of what this cleanup removed, why each\n  removal is safe, and how to get any of it back — the repo had no\n  written trace of a 16.7k-line deletion.\n\nVerified locally: cargo test green, vitest 859/859, tsc 0, biome clean,\nvite build succeeds (all nine weather glyphs still emit as real assets).\ntauri.conf.json names only the five icons that remain, so the deleted\nios/android/windows sets were genuinely unbundled.\n\nNot fixed, deliberately:\n- vendor/shared-ui/design/tokens.css still cites the deleted mock for\n  --media-mint''s hex. It is a vendored file under a pinned SHA-256\n  snapshot guard, and the citation is provenance, not a live contract.\n- The BrightData token is not rotated (PR-Agent, high). It is the\n  operator''s explicitly accepted risk: free-tier key, in history since\n  7430b4b, closure note says re-file only if the account goes paid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"314128a8155efd83046e892b2d16a349f6203aff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/314128a8155efd83046e892b2d16a349f6203aff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/f7475009466764d0eaf355fa8b661b10159e6665","verification":{"payload":"tree 314128a8155efd83046e892b2d16a349f6203aff\nparent 74ac8cbc6019ae43548db8f87c1d14e34a923130\nauthor Chetan Jain <JAIN.CJ.CHETAN@gmail.com> 1785773140 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785773140 +0530\n\nchore: consolidate repository references and AI tooling (#18)\n\n* chore: consolidate repository references and AI tooling\n\n* docs: close the cleanup''s review findings\n\nSix fixes from the PR #18 review round (CodeRabbit x2, own pass x4):\n\n- .gitignore: the comment named a \"root `skills` symlink\" that does not\n  exist; the one tracked path is `.agents/skills` (CodeRabbit).\n- prototype/weather-art.html: the body lede still said the glyphs were\n  \"vendored locally\" after the page moved to loading them from\n  ../src/assets/weather/ (CodeRabbit).\n- the tab-notch spec still declared the two deleted mocks \"Design\n  sources of truth (binding)\", with a tie-break rule (\"the mock wins\"\n  on values) that nothing could honor once they were gone. Shipped\n  src/ is authoritative now; the mocks are recorded as historical\n  provenance, retrievable via git log and branch\n  feat/tab-notch-redesign.\n- plan 065''s closure had been quietly reopened: the cleanup addendum\n  read as \"rotation is still required\", contradicting the operator''s\n  recorded accepted-risk decision and dropping its do-not-re-file\n  guard. Restored in both plans/README.md and the plan file, with the\n  working-tree removal recorded as a side effect that changes nothing\n  about the acceptance.\n- CLAUDE.md: added a record of what this cleanup removed, why each\n  removal is safe, and how to get any of it back — the repo had no\n  written trace of a 16.7k-line deletion.\n\nVerified locally: cargo test green, vitest 859/859, tsc 0, biome clean,\nvite build succeeds (all nine weather glyphs still emit as real assets).\ntauri.conf.json names only the five icons that remain, so the deleted\nios/android/windows sets were genuinely unbundled.\n\nNot fixed, deliberately:\n- vendor/shared-ui/design/tokens.css still cites the deleted mock for\n  --media-mint''s hex. It is a vendored file under a pinned SHA-256\n  snapshot guard, and the citation is provenance, not a live contract.\n- The BrightData token is not rotated (PR-Agent, high). It is the\n  operator''s explicitly accepted risk: free-tier key, in history since\n  7430b4b, closure note says re-file only if the account goes paid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcLxUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4okQAJK0yRDOuipeLu2pIF6zzD6R\nBK8voniWbb1DTdfZ+wZkI/zbbMr9aPU/2bdgrM1xSMS3ub2t/D1EpoTAE6GIFl5F\n/V/1PPxVbQ2sYIkAdq81i99ApUmyEz/2Y74BgyEx6ignUX0UDWK7xLPoeC4ODrfP\n0a0ziOuI4uqUdo7YWNByV37PDz4iTO+6Vqy2CUZUgdKA65UscqtUeesT