organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/fdf9cf69851646480c36535e42c31694c831bfe8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T20:17:25Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T20:17:25Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"test(tabs): rejection cases, App seam, identity parity pin\n\nPlan 180. Backfills the coverage plan 171''s tab-notch work left open,\nplus the one production fix its two validators needed.\n\n- useStatusState: 5 rejection tests for the four clauses plan 171 added\n  (missing/non-object `agent`, a bad `activeSessions`, `chargeFraction`\n  outside its `[0,1]` range — the file''s only range check — a negative\n  `chargeCount`, a non-boolean `isCharged`), plus an inclusive-boundary\n  acceptance. The validator is all-or-nothing, so one bad field from\n  rust blanks the whole status rail with nothing naming the cause.\n- iconPresence: the `iconPresenceFor(undefined)` early return, asserted\n  equal to the QUIET table so the settings preview and the live overlay\n  cannot disagree.\n- App: the seam for `useTabSelection`''s one production call site. Drop\n  the `selectedTab` prop or mistype the channel and the overlay degrades\n  to \"clicking an icon does nothing\" with the suite still green.\n- New `src/tabWireParity.test.ts`: a text-level, region-scoped pin\n  (`hookEventParity.test.ts`''s idiom) over the five-tab identity set''s\n  six hand-synced sites. The drift it catches is silent by construction\n  — `useTabSelection` coerces an unrecognised token to `selected: null`,\n  a real and expected value, so rust-side drift renders as a working app\n  that never selects anything.\n- ShortcutsSection: `/\\s/` -> the explicit Unicode `White_Space` class,\n  so the TS mirror matches `settings.rs::is_valid_prefix_shortcut`''s\n  `char::is_whitespace` exactly. They disagreed in both directions:\n  U+0085 (NEL) passed the UI and failed the save; U+FEFF did the\n  reverse. Both sides now run the same fixture table, and both run a\n  full-BMP sweep so the 25-code-point class is machine-checked rather\n  than eyeballed.\n\nSuites: 1048 rust (+2), 842 frontend (+29). `docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md`\n§0 recounted live — that recount absorbs every plan merged since the\n171 row, not only this one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec0165afd9333a7b0dc688a9d1162873ce65de26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/ec0165afd9333a7b0dc688a9d1162873ce65de26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/fdf9cf69851646480c36535e42c31694c831bfe8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/u