,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T19:31:29Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"fix(tabs): grow the hovered flank with icon count so clicks land on their glyphs\n\nPlan 175. Plan 171 shipped the icon strip''s rust hit-test geometry paired\nagainst a design mock instead of against the CSS that eventually shipped,\nand left a \"re-pair these against the real stylesheet once it exists\"\nnote. The two had drifted in both terms: the CSS painted a flat 85px\nflank with a 16px inset, rust computed max(85*scale, 26n+14) with a 14px\none. At 3+ present tabs the rects slid right of the painted glyphs (~9px\nat 3, ~35px at 4, ~61px at 5, against a 26px pitch), so a click on a\nvisible icon selected the wrong tab or nothing — and the flank''s\n`overflow: hidden` clipped the leftmost glyphs out of view entirely.\n\nThe reconciliation runs in the direction the mock intended: the CSS\nadopts the icon-count-driven growth (a flat 85px flank can never fit 4-5\nicons), and the inset unifies on the CSS''s shipped 16 (rust moves 14->16;\nzero visual change).\n\n- hover.rs: FLANK_INSET 14 -> 16, and the constants comment now names its\n  three real lockstep twins instead of the frozen mock.\n- StatusRailCard.tsx: threads `--present-icons` onto `.card-assembly`,\n  counted off the same `iconPresenceFor` table IconStrip renders from —\n  no second presence predicate. It agrees with rust''s `present_tabs`,\n  including the paused-but-loaded track case.\n- card-chrome.css: the two `--cw` rules that can match while the strip is\n  up now compute `max(85px * scale, (26n + 16) * 1px)`, symmetric on both\n  flanks to match rust''s `cutout + 2 * flank_w` and the `1fr auto 1fr`\n  grid. `--present-icons` defaults to 0, which collapses each rule back\n  to the pre-175 formula.\n- stripGeometryParity.test.ts: a text-level pin across all three sites,\n  same cheap register as hookEventParity.test.ts.\n\nGates: cargo test 1044 lib + 3 integration + 3 doc, clippy -D warnings\nclean, vitest 818/818, tsc and biome ci clean. Test counts recounted live\nin TESTING_STRATEGY.md §0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2fe2f1ee9c066c6375f4eba3078093d8a9a6de8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/2fe2f1ee9c066c6375f4eba3078093d8a9a6de8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/d01204f967d5ab1cb47ee57b5a12601205cfd958","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/d01204f967d5ab1cb47ee57b5a12601205cfd958","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKGQwMTIwNGY5NjdkNWFiMWNiNDdlZTU3YjVhMTI2MDEyMDVjZmQ5NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/12e32e498d59651679f3b5d0fb3a7635c7fce0e4","sha":"12e32e498d59651679f3b5d0fb3a7635c7fce0e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/12e32e498d59651679f3b5d0fb3a7635c7fce0e4"}],"sha":"d01204f967d5ab1cb47ee57b5a12601205cfd958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/d01204f967d5ab1cb47ee57b5a12601205cfd958"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/71d83f6995cb1d55cee8a32b629d836ba43da962/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T19:30:23Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T19:30:23Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"fix(hover): poison-tolerant lock in on_mouse_moved (reviewer-authorized twin of the :550 site)\n\nThe `on_mouse_entered` twin of this line was fixed in the previous\ncommit as one of plan 179''s three listed sites; this one is identical,\nin the sibling tracking-area closure, and is the hotter path (mouseMoved\nfires many times per second). Both run on the AppKit main thread, so the\nsame reasoning applies: a poisoning panic elsewhere must not turn every\nlater mouse event into a panic unwinding inside an objc callback.\n\nPlan 179 named only the `:550` site and its \"Out of scope\" section bars\na wider `.lock().unwrap()` sweep, so this was flagged rather than fixed\nduring execution; the reviewer authorized it as a scope amendment.\n\nNo comment added at the site — the policy note lives at the first site\nin `hover_point_is_over_card`. Behaviour-preserving; test counts\nunchanged (1043 + 3 + 3), clippy clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f85fda0edc607064f1452345031a0f0769735878","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/f85fda0edc607064f1452345031a0f0769735878"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/71d83f6995cb1d55cee8a32b629d836ba43da962","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/71d83f6995cb1d55cee8a32b629d836ba43da962","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKDcxZDgzZjY5OTVjYjFkNTVjZWU4YTMyYjYyOWQ4MzZiYTQzZGE5NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/04e49ad9cf557ac496210f8d5bb7479536ab474c","sha":"04e49ad9cf557ac496210f8d5bb7479536ab474c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/04e49ad9cf557ac496210f8d5bb7479536ab474c"}],"sha":"71d83f6995cb1d55cee8a32b629d836ba43da962","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/71d83f6995cb1d55cee8a32b629d836ba43da962"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/f1196074e03fde076e1c34e15d6acd9ed8fd28e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T19:29:54Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T19:29:54Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"fix(prefix): deadline-aware watchdog + self-healing forced release\n\nPlan 178. Two flaws defeated the prefix keymap''s own dead-man''s switch,\nthe thing that keeps a wedged bare `Enter` grab from breaking the user''s\ntyping in every application until notchtap restarts.\n\n1. Every arm spawned a watchdog that slept 5s then force-released\n   unconditionally, so an ordinary \"hesitate, time out, try again\"\n   rhythm (arm at t0, re-arm at t0+4s) let the FIRST arm''s watchdog fire\n   mid-way through the SECOND arm''s live window and silently release its\n   grabs. `TabWire` now records `last_arm_at`, and the watchdog is a\n   verdict-driven loop: it defers to any newer arm still inside its own\n   budget instead of killing it. The watchdog stays generation-BLIND on\n   purpose — a generation gate would blind it to the \"follow-up\n   consumed, but its release failed\" case only it can catch — so the fix\n   is a time deadline, not a generation check.\n\n2. `force_release_prefix_followups` cleared `followups_registered` first\n   and discarded the release result, so a partially failed release left\n   the flag lying \"released\": every later watchdog early-returned on it\n   and the grab stuck until restart. It now restores the flag on\n   failure, honouring the invariant `handle_prefix_fire` and\n   `handle_prefix_followup` already keep, which makes the loop retry.\n\nAll watchdog policy lives in a pure `watchdog_verdict` (house\npure-decision/thin-apply pattern) with a seven-case table test; the\nasync loop stays untested by design rather than adding a third\nreal-timer async test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"abbff9be23e5ff28c1001535057a405e8c5062ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/abbff9be23e5ff28c1001535057a405e8c5062ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/f1196074e03fde076e1c34e15d6acd9ed8fd28e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/f1196074e03fde076e1c34e15d6acd9ed8fd28e4","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKGYxMTk2MDc0ZTAzZmRlMDc2ZTFjMzRlMTVkNmFjZDllZDhmZDI4ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/12e32e498d59651679f3b5d0fb3a7635c7fce0e4","sha":"12e32e498d59651679f3b5d0fb3a7635c7fce0e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/12e32e498d59651679f3b5d0fb3a7635c7fce0e4"}],"sha":"f1196074e03fde076e1c34e15d6acd9ed8fd28e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/f1196074e03fde076e1c34e15d6acd9ed8fd28e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/04e49ad9cf557ac496210f8d5bb7479536ab474c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T19:27:58Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T19:27:58Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"fix(input): live card_scale, poison-tolerant AppKit locks, ordered tab emit\n\nPlan 179. Three defects in the plan-171 input path, batched because they\nshare files and the theme that the native input path must not trust boot\nstate or panic across FFI.\n\n1. The click monitor froze `card_scale` at boot. `ClickMonitorParams`\n   loses its `scale` field and the handler reads the managed `Config`\n   per event, the way `hover_point_is_over_card` already does — so a\n   hot-applied Appearance scale change (`set_appearance`) moves the\n   click rects together with the hover rects and the webview, instead\n   of leaving clicks missing visible icons until a relaunch.\n\n2. Three lock sites reachable from AppKit callbacks used `.unwrap()`:\n   `hover_point_is_over_card`''s config read, the tracking area''s\n   `was_hovered` read, and `emit_hover_changed_if_transitioned`''s\n   guard. The `Config` mutex is genuinely poisonable (it is held across\n   `write_config_atomic`), and a poisoning panic would have turned every\n   later mouse event into a panic unwinding inside an objc callback.\n   Now poison-tolerant, matching house policy in these same paths.\n\n3. `tab-selection-changed` was emitted after its dedup lock was dropped,\n   with two writer threads — click/prefix on the AppKit main thread and\n   the engine status loop on a tokio worker. An interleave could put the\n   older payload on the wire last, and the mismatch stuck because the\n   next call compares against the newer guard value and returns early.\n   The emit now runs under the guard, making wire order a total order\n   under that mutex; `app.emit` is a synchronous non-blocking post, so\n   this adds no blocking edge.\n\nBehaviour-preserving outside those exact interleavings; no test-count\nchange (1043 + 3 + 3 rust, 813 web, clippy clean).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"105c502c506730675a208a4816dc3796f9fdb865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/105c502c506730675a208a4816dc3796f9fdb865"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/04e49ad9cf557ac496210f8d5bb7479536ab474c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"ht