fix_followups_registered, force_release_prefix_followups,\nhandle_prefix_fire, handle_prefix_followup, and the RunEvent::Exit cleanup) used\ntauri_plugin_global_shortcut types (Code/Shortcut/Modifiers) and the global_shortcut()\nextension method without the cfg gate every other consumer of that macOS-only target\ndependency already carries. CI''s rust job only runs on macos-latest so this never broke\nCI, but it broke cargo build/test on non-macOS dev environments. Gated to match the\nfile''s existing convention.","tree":{"sha":"29362ec4762288c4282f93f821a1e5914a9f7c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/29362ec4762288c4282f93f821a1e5914a9f7c07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/7ca82d5d67497fbac2b49486447cf7175fe18f95","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/7ca82d5d67497fbac2b49486447cf7175fe18f95","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKDdjYTgyZDVkNjc0OTdmYmFjMmI0OTQ4NjQ0N2NmNzE3NWZlMThmOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/0e9b212bb5b2ae76594a6705e0a1b1e0edbcc0ea","sha":"0e9b212bb5b2ae76594a6705e0a1b1e0edbcc0ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/0e9b212bb5b2ae76594a6705e0a1b1e0edbcc0ea"}],"sha":"7ca82d5d67497fbac2b49486447cf7175fe18f95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/7ca82d5d67497fbac2b49486447cf7175fe18f95"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/0e9b212bb5b2ae76594a6705e0a1b1e0edbcc0ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T15:00:33Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T15:00:33Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"docs: record plan 171''s decisions, vocabulary, and shortcuts (post-merge truth pass)\n\nPR #13 shipped real behaviour that four load-bearing docs didn''t\ndescribe. Each gap below was found by checking the doc against the code,\nnot by assuming.\n\n- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §22 (new) — this file holds the LOCKED\n  decisions, and had no tab-notch entry at all. Records the pull-vs-push\n  precedence rule, the bare-rest/visibility-hidden choice (load-bearing\n  twice: it reserves the strip''s width AND is why every `infinite` icon\n  animation must be gated on `.hovered`), the max-one selection model,\n  and the two hazardous mechanisms with the reason each is shaped the way\n  it is: the NSEvent click monitor (not a preference — a webview onClick\n  cannot reach the rust-owned selection through a capability file that\n  grants only listen/unlisten) and the temporary bare-key grabs (a failed\n  register is benign, a failed unregister is not).\n- `CONTEXT.md` — the spec introduces vocabulary in its own §1 and the\n  glossary had NONE of it. Adds Icon Strip, Tab Selection, Pull, Prefix,\n  News Charge.\n- `CLAUDE.md` — the ipc/security section said the overlay is receive-only\n  with no click handlers. Still true, but now misleading: there IS a\n  click path. Documents how it preserves the boundary, and says plainly\n  that wanting an `invoke` for a click is the signal you''re about to\n  break it, not a gap to fill.\n- `README.md` — the shortcut table was missing two long-shipped combos\n  (⌃⇧] skip, ⌃⇧, settings) and the entire prefix keymap.\n- `docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md` §0 — recounted live after the merge:\n  944->1037 lib-crate (+93 with plan 171), row total 1040; frontend\n  573->793. §0 is the only place counts may live, so it''s the only place\n  changed.\n\nVerified every path referenced in the new §22 resolves. Gates: cargo\nfmt/clippy clean, vitest 793, tsc/biome clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"447d7aeaad1a8caf1cf79fec9908ff062d83c811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/447d7aeaad1a8caf1cf79fec9908ff062d83