,"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/9b99bb6e58d1efa90f1f532d66cdf8bd1516d51f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T12:21:25Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T12:21:25Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"feat(football): crossbar persistent variant (plan 171, slice G)\n\nExtracted the score-block markup into ScoreBlockContent (verbatim, no\nbehavior change) so the crossbar variant''s second, stacked block can\nreuse it instead of a drifting copy. Added FootballHeroCard''s\nsecondaryMatches prop (default []) — every existing caller renders\nbyte-identical to before (143 pre-existing tests unchanged), 6 new\ntests cover the stacked block: renders, carries its own league/pill/\nclock/score, its own independent cardsClean, stable non-index keys\nacross multiple secondary matches.\n\nDeliberately no separate `crossbar` boolean — that state is fully\nexpressed by which `title` string the caller passes plus whether\nsecondaryMatches is non-empty; a redundant flag would just restate\ncaller-controlled information.\n\nFlagged, not improvised: nothing on the wire currently surfaces more\nthan one live match at a time (StatusState.football.live is a single\nOption; poller.rs''s own snapshot map already tracks every watched\nleague but collapses to \"first in-play wins\" before the wire). This\nslice''s file scope (NotificationBody.tsx only) doesn''t cover the rust\nwire change a real second match would need — left for Slice K''s\nintegration or a dedicated follow-up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc1921e5f64643d32055a7a7ac9ed271bf585d38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/dc192