https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/4af9ba3dcc0494b7d0d369b62ace62e7375951f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:07:52Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:07:52Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"docs(plans): mark click detection as an operator hand-off to the Mac Mini\n\nNot blocking the rest of the plan -- frontend slices (E-J) and the\nnon-AppKit-specific rust logic in slices B-D don''t depend on it and\ncontinue on the Linux side in the meantime; only slice A''s remaining\nitems (3/4) and slice K''s integration wait on this being resolved on\nreal hardware.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e5b07407b982b540a9f20ee06d25a3ec778fd97a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/e5b07407b982b540a9f20ee06d25a3ec778fd97a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/4af9ba3dcc0494b7d0d369b62ace62e7375951f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/4af9ba3dcc0494b7d0d369b62ace62e7375951f8","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKDRhZjliYTNkY2MwNDk0YjdkMGQzNjliNjJhY2U2MmU3Mzc1OTUxZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/0881b17e2d15639fee7589a6882244f2db39ec7f","sha":"0881b17e2d15639fee7589a6882244f2db39ec7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/0881b17e2d15639fee7589a6882244f2db39ec7f"}],"sha":"4af9ba3dcc0494b7d0d369b62ace62e7375951f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/4af9ba3dcc0494b7d0d369b62ace62e7375951f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/0881b17e2d15639fee7589a6882244f2db39ec7f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:02:20Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:02:20Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"docs(plans): flag click-detection mechanism as a genuine open question (slice A)\n\nInvestigated wiring click-through + click detection into the live hover\npath and found a real, unresolved design fork: panel_event! (from the\nthird-party tauri-nspanel crate) only exposes mouseEntered/mouseMoved/\nmouseExited, confirmed by reading its actual call sites -- no click\ncallback exists. Two candidate mechanisms (a new native NSEvent local\nmonitor, vs. relying on plain webview onClick once click-through is off)\nare both plausible but neither is verifiable from this Linux dev\nenvironment, and guessing wrong would mean shipping a nontrivial amount\nof native code that might not even fire.\n\nBacked out two premature pieces rather than land them half-finished:\n- A speculative Cargo.toml dependency addition (block2, objc2-app-kit''s\n  NSEvent feature) for a monitor that was never actually written.\n- Wiring a broadened click-through trigger into the live\n  emit_hover_changed_if_transitioned path ahead of any click handling --\n  landing that alone would be a real regression (idle-hover would start\n  silently eating clicks that today pass through to the desktop, e.g.\n  during the weather peek, with zero compensating functionality yet).\n\nFixed two stale doc comments (in lib.rs and tabs.rs) that referenced a\nclick monitor as if it existed, caught during self-review before commit.\n\nplans/171 updated with the specific recommendation: settle this\nempirically on real macOS hardware (mount a NonactivatingPanel, disable\nclick-through, check with a devtools console.log in onClick whether a\nreal click reaches the webview) before writing more code toward either\nanswer.\n\ncargo fmt applied. 966/966 cargo test passing, unchanged from the prior\ncommit -- this commit is docs + comment fixes + a clean revert, no new\nruntime behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d5ae43b9465882f12b4315cffb037988cfdd9ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/0d5ae43b9465882f12b4315cffb037988cfdd9ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/0881b17e2d15639fee7589a6882244f2db39ec7f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/0881b17e2d15639fee7589a6882244f2db39ec7f","node_id":"C_kwDOTabiVNoAKDA4ODFiMTdlMmQxNTYzOWZlZTc1ODlhNjg4MjI0NGYyZGIzOWVjN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81/notchtap/commit/4443469fa20650991c761c4a4e8a5f0c130160cd","sha":"4443469fa20650991c761c4a4e8a5f0c130160cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/4443469fa20650991c761c4a4e8a5f0c130160cd"}],"sha":"0881b17e2d15639fee7589a6882244f2db39ec7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/0881b17e2d15639fee7589a6882244f2db39ec7f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jainChetan81","id":38555207,"login":"jainChetan81","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTU1MjA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/commits/5c524531f17a57c834f0a2969e224ea6a6e20ba5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:55:33Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:55:33Z","email":"jain.cj.chetan@gmail.com","name":"jainChetan81"},"message":"feat(settings): tonal status chips, tactile press feedback, adapter tile redesign\n\nColorful pills, not monochrome ones: MetaChip gains a `tone` prop\n(positive/caution/critical/accent) reusing the overlay''s own\n--overlay-green/amber/coral/teal accents, so status actually reads by\ncolor instead of needing the label read in full. Applied to the\nConnectors secret-status chip and the Agents adapter health chip (now\ntri-state: available/partial/unavailable, not a binary active flag).\n\nPriority pickers across Agents/Football/General/News/Weather now color\ntheir selected segment with the same low/medium/high accent scheme the\noverlay''s own priority-accent system already uses, instead of a flat\nneutral highlight — one consistent color language end to end.\n\nButtons, the switch track, and segmented controls get real tactile\npress feedback (layered scale + inset shadow, not just a 1px nudge) —\naddresses the \"buttons feel shallow\" complaint directly.\n\nThe Agent adapter tiles (Claude Code/Codex/Kimi/OpenCode) collapse by\ndefault and expand on click to reveal real fields — last seen, last\nerror, capabilities as a labeled list, the setup snippet — instead of\nalways-visible tag/pill clutter. Modeled on Handy''s (handy.computer)\nown per-model status clarity, extended beyond the narrower Agents-only\nproposal already in prototypes/future-proposal.html.\n\nTTL bar fill/trough bumped for legibility while preserving the\ndocumented >=2.5x contrast-separation ratio between held and active\nstates.\n\nAlso: two new whole-app prototype references (prototypes/full-app-\ncurrent-state.html, full-app-future-vision.html) covering the overlay\n+ full settings sidebar and a Handy-informed whole-product roadmap\nincluding agent-pipeline batching/live-feel ideas; prototype/agent-\nboard.html and prototypes/current-state.html resynced against the\nboard-motion-polish merge and the two new Agents toggles.\n\n625 vitest tests passing, tsc clean, biome clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7636f223e661b7df2d6ff0078d8e93a419b54da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/trees/e7636f223e661b7df2d6ff0078d8e93a419b54da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jainChetan81/notchtap/git/commits/5c524531f17a57c834f0a2969e224ea6a6e20ba5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38555207?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jainChetan81/events{/privacy}","followers_url