hor":{"date":"2026-07-20T19:54:01Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T19:54:01Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"docs: update changelog, AGENTS.md, and docs for 0.1.0 release\n\nAdd missing entries for dashboard restart banner, dashboard status\nendpoint, config endpoint, DashboardStatusContext, and\nuseDashboardRollout hook across CHANGELOG, AGENTS.md, BFF_PATTERN,\nPROJECT_LAYOUT, and OPENSHIFT_DEPLOY docs. Fix stale namespace-summary\nreferences in LOCAL_SETUP. Mark all phases complete in PROJECT_PLAN\nand split open questions into resolved vs open.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9accb44ede050cd847b5f046b6b3522219af6e08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/9accb44ede050cd847b5f046b6b3522219af6e08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/f4ac710db39afc6f012231e47ccdbb20df539a02","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/f4ac710db39afc6f012231e47ccdbb20df539a02","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKGY0YWM3MTBkYjM5YWZjNmYwMTIyMzFlNDdjY2RiYjIwZGY1MzlhMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/54e7156eab3b2c7d9b3ee21effafb10f81c1dfd6","sha":"54e7156eab3b2c7d9b3ee21effafb10f81c1dfd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/54e7156eab3b2c7d9b3ee21effafb10f81c1dfd6"}],"sha":"f4ac710db39afc6f012231e47ccdbb20df539a02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/f4ac710db39afc6f012231e47ccdbb20df539a02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/54e7156eab3b2c7d9b3ee21effafb10f81c1dfd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T19:30:37Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T19:30:37Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"fix: harden lifecycle operations, catalog freshness, and post-action UX\n\n- Fix BFF lifecycle endpoints: SSE streaming, Helm namespace discovery,\n  route validation, MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG format preservation, and\n  rollback on failed installs\n- Ensure catalog data is always fresh: bust BFF in-memory cache on every\n  page navigation and bypass GitHub CDN cache with no-cache headers\n- Add live dashboard rollout monitoring after config-changing operations\n  (install, remove, enable, disable) with a polling banner that tracks\n  pod restart progress\n- Show the Upgrade button only when the installed Helm version differs\n  from the catalog version\n- Update plugin.yaml with actual maintainer info and image repositories\n- Fix documentation discrepancies found by codebase audit\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7a2574389ba85650e2d6b353b0dd2ec8527b2e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/e7a2574389ba85650e2d6b353b0dd2ec8527b2e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/54e7156eab3b2c7d9b3ee21effafb10f81c1dfd6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/54e7156eab3b2c7d9b3ee21effafb10f81c1dfd6","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKDU0ZTcxNTZlYWIzYjJjN2Q5YjNlZTIxZWZmYWZiMTBmODFjMWRmZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/ed2041f5d67980e66a8cdd21c42f0eb3e1729224","sha":"ed2041f5d67980e66a8cdd21c42f0eb3e1729224","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/ed2041f5d67980e66a8cdd21c42f0eb3e1729224"}],"sha":"54e7156eab3b2c7d9b3ee21effafb10f81c1dfd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/54e7156eab3b2c7d9b3ee21effafb10f81c1dfd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/ed2041f5d67980e66a8cdd21c42f0eb3e1729224/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T21:51:06Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T21:51:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 8 — Testing, Polish & Documentation (#96)\n\n* feat: add error boundary, 404 route, and accessibility improvements\n\n- Add React ErrorBoundary in App.tsx with recovery UI\n- Add catch-all route redirecting unknown paths to catalog\n- Change content wrapper from div to main for landmark navigation\n- Add role=\"status\" to CommunityBanner for screen readers\n- Replace hardcoded #fff with PF token for banner text color\n- Add \"Browse Catalog\" button to InstalledPage empty state\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update architecture docs, project layout, and README for Phases 1-7\n\n- CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md: add all 12 hooks, lifecycle BFF endpoints, new\n  services, components, types, utils, and Helm chart RBAC resources\n- BFF_PATTERN.md: rewrite with current directory structure, all endpoints,\n  services architecture, RBAC permissions, and lifecycle operations\n- PROJECT_LAYOUT.md: update full directory tree with BFF routes/services,\n  frontend hooks/types/components, and chart templates\n- README.md: add BFF API reference table and lifecycle operations docs\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add comprehensive test coverage for Phase 8\n\nBFF tests (23 new):\n- Health endpoint test\n- installPlugin, enablePlugin, disablePlugin service unit tests\n- Enable/disable route error path tests (401, 400, 500)\n- buildCatalogPlugin field mapping coverage (install, rbac, remote,\n  deploymentModel, bffImage, support)\n\nFrontend tests (11 new):\n- App.tsx error boundary catch and recovery tests\n- App.tsx main landmark test\n- PluginDetailModal lifecycle button click assertions (install, upgrade,\n  remove, disable)\n- ConfirmRemoveModal loading state test\n- LifecycleProgressModal in-progress state test\n- InstalledPage \"Browse Catalog\" button in empty state\n\nFix: use isAriaDisabled instead of isDisabled on LifecycleProgressModal\nfooter button to keep the element tabbable for PatternFly''s focus trap.\n\nFix: markdownlint blank-line-around-lists in BFF_PATTERN.md.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Remove incorrect role=\"status\" from CommunityBanner — the banner is\n  static content, not a live region. A plain div is appropriate here.\n- Add componentDidCatch to ErrorBoundary for error logging. Without it,\n  runtime errors were silently swallowed with no diagnostic output.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Fix hook count in AGENTS.md: \"Twelve\" → \"Eleven\" (actual count)\n- Fix false claim in BFF_PATTERN.md that BFF uses ServiceAccount token\n  for Helm operations — it always uses the user''s forwarded token\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lifecycle): guard Close button click during in-progress operations (#102)\n\nisAriaDisabled only sets aria-disabled on the DOM element and does not\nsuppress click events. Guard the onClick handler so that clicking Close\nwhile an operation is running is a no-op, preventing premature teardown\nof UI state while the BFF Helm operation continues asynchronously.\n\nAdd a test to verify the click is suppressed during in-progress state.\n\nFixes #97\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tests): restore monkey-patched mocks in afterEach to prevent leaks (#103)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(app): nested main landmark, error boundary remount, and import aliases (#104)\n\n* fix(app): nested main landmark, error boundary remount, and import aliases\n\n- Replace <main> with <div> to avoid nested landmarks in dashboard host\n- Add retryKey to ErrorBoundary to force child remount on \"Try again\"\n- Convert relative imports to ~ path alias per project conventions\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use React.Fragment for retryKey wrapper to avoid extra DOM node\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2a90a6035cb2e42098140d2cb4a9d320beddea2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/b2a90a6035cb2e42098140d2cb4a9d320beddea2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/ed2041f5d67980e66a8cdd21c42f0eb3e1729224","verification":{"payload":"tree b2a90a6035cb2e42098140d2cb4a9d320beddea2\nparent 2073726c17ace08c4c332e34d8955ca1c5601878\nparent 04c9727c680a55d731f19f0171393029947d4999\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784325066 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784325066 -0400\n\nfeat: Phase 8 — Testing, Polish & Documentation (#96)\n\n* feat: add error boundary, 404 route, and accessibility improvements\n\n- Add React ErrorBoundary in App.tsx with recovery UI\n- Add catch-all route redirecting unknown paths to catalog\n- Change content wrapper from div to main for landmark navigation\n- Add role=\"status\" to CommunityBanner for screen readers\n- Replace hardcoded #fff with PF token for banner text color\n- Add \"Browse Catalog\" button to InstalledPage empty state\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update architecture docs, project layout, and README for Phases 1-7\n\n- CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md: add all 12 hooks, lifecycle BFF endpoints, new\n  services, components, types, utils, and Helm chart RBAC resources\n- BFF_PATTERN.md: rewrite with current directory structure, all endpoints,\n  services architecture, RBAC permissions, and lifecycle operations\n- PROJECT_LAYOUT.md: update full directory tree with BFF routes/services,\n  frontend hooks/types/components, and chart templates\n- README.md: add BFF API reference table and lifecycle operations docs\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add comprehensive test coverage for Phase 8\n\nBFF tests (23 new):\n- Health endpoint test\n- installPlugin, enablePlugin, disablePlugin service unit tests\n- Enable/disable route error path tests (401, 400, 500)\n- buildCatalogPlugin field mapping coverage (install, rbac, remote,\n  deploymentModel, bffImage, support)\n\nFrontend tests (11 new):\n- App.tsx error boundary catch and recovery tests\n- App.tsx main landmark test\n- PluginDetailModal lifecycle button click assertions (install, upgrade,\n  remove, disable)\n- ConfirmRemoveModal loading state test\n- LifecycleProgressModal in-progress state test\n- InstalledPage \"Browse Catalog\" button in empty state\n\nFix: use isAriaDisabled instead of isDisabled on LifecycleProgressModal\nfooter button to keep the element tabbable for PatternFly''s focus trap.\n\nFix: markdownlint blank-line-around-lists in BFF_PATTERN.md.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Remove incorrect role=\"status\" from CommunityBanner — the banner is\n  static content, not a live region. A plain div is appropriate here.\n- Add componentDidCatch to ErrorBoundary for error logging. Without it,\n  runtime errors were silently swallowed with no diagnostic output.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Fix hook count in AGENTS.md: \"Twelve\" → \"Eleven\" (actual count)\n- Fix false claim in BFF_PATTERN.md that BFF uses ServiceAccount token\n  for Helm operations — it always uses the user''s forwarded token\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lifecycle): guard Close button click during in-progress operations (#102)\n\nisAriaDisabled only sets aria-disabled on the DOM element and does not\nsuppress click events. Guard the onClick handler so that clicking Close\nwhile an operation is running is a no-op, preventing premature teardown\nof UI state while the BFF Helm operation continues asynchronously.\n\nAdd a test to verify the click is suppressed during in-progress state.\n\nFixes #97\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tests): restore monkey-patched mocks in afterEach to prevent leaks (#103)\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\n