outier"},"message":"feat: add error boundary, 404 route, and accessibility improvements\n\n- Add React ErrorBoundary in App.tsx with recovery UI\n- Add catch-all route redirecting unknown paths to catalog\n- Change content wrapper from div to main for landmark navigation\n- Add role=\"status\" to CommunityBanner for screen readers\n- Replace hardcoded #fff with PF token for banner text color\n- Add \"Browse Catalog\" button to InstalledPage empty state\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f49f728580b9f1bb1dfc1dab0c52f08ac5e1142a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/f49f728580b9f1bb1dfc1dab0c52f08ac5e1142a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/5be27b379319e92105f1c2ccb8cd8f12c0be3001","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/5be27b379319e92105f1c2ccb8cd8f12c0be3001","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKDViZTI3YjM3OTMxOWU5MjEwNWYxYzJjY2I4Y2Q4ZjEyYzBiZTMwMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/2073726c17ace08c4c332e34d8955ca1c5601878","sha":"2073726c17ace08c4c332e34d8955ca1c5601878","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/2073726c17ace08c4c332e34d8955ca1c5601878"}],"sha":"5be27b379319e92105f1c2ccb8cd8f12c0be3001","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/5be27b379319e92105f1c2ccb8cd8f12c0be3001"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/2073726c17ace08c4c332e34d8955ca1c5601878/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:51:08Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:51:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 7 — Helm Chart & Deployment Updates (#85)\n\n* feat(chart): add RBAC, configurable values, and CI/CD updates for Phase 7\n\n- Add ClusterRole and ClusterRoleBinding for BFF ServiceAccount with\n  permissions to manage plugin lifecycle operations (dashboard config\n  patching, namespace management, Helm-deployed resources)\n- Add bffServiceAccountName helper to _helpers.tpl\n- Expose charter registry URL, cache TTLs, and fetch concurrency as\n  configurable Helm values with env var injection in BFF deployment\n- Add bff.rbac.create toggle (default: true)\n- Update plugin.yaml rbac section with required cluster role declarations\n- Add Helm chart linting job to CI workflow\n- Add dev branch to CI triggers\n- Update OPENSHIFT_DEPLOY.md with RBAC documentation and new Helm values\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Always set serviceAccountName on BFF deployment (fixes pre-existing SA\n  pattern where create=false + name=my-sa silently fell back to default)\n- Remove redundant secrets rule from ClusterRole (already covered by core\n  resources rule)\n- Scope RBAC to namespace-scoped roles/rolebindings only instead of\n  cluster-scoped (prevents privilege escalation via ClusterRole creation)\n- Consolidate overlapping deployments rules into single rule\n- Sync plugin.yaml RBAC declarations with actual ClusterRole rules\n- Update deployment docs RBAC table to match\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Add template guard preventing ClusterRole binding to the ''default''\n  ServiceAccount — helm template now fails with a clear message when\n  bff.rbac.create=true but no SA is configured\n- Add bff.serviceAccount.name to Helm Chart Reference table in docs\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): disable SA token auto-mount in BFF pod spec (#91)\n\nThe BFF never reads the SA token — all Kubernetes API calls and Helm\noperations use the end user''s forwarded Bearer token. Setting\nautomountServiceAccountToken: false on the pod spec removes the\nunnecessarily mounted token and reduces the attack surface.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): add update/patch verbs to ClusterRole namespace rule (#92)\n\nThe namespaces rule was missing update and patch verbs, which are\nrequired when a community plugin''s Helm chart includes a Namespace\nresource directly. Without these verbs, helm upgrade would fail with\n403 Forbidden when reconciling changes on namespace objects.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): check source values instead of resolved name in RBAC fail guard (#93)\n\nReplaces the resolved-name check (`eq $saName \"default\"`) with a\nsource-values check so that explicitly naming a ServiceAccount \"default\"\nwith `bff.serviceAccount.create=true` is no longer incorrectly blocked.\nThe dangerous case — `bff.serviceAccount.create=false` with no name set —\nstill fails as expected.\n\nFixes #90\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): separate secrets into own ClusterRole rule without watch verb (#94)\n\nSplits secrets out of the bundled core resources rule and removes the\nwatch verb, which is not needed for Helm lifecycle operations. This\nreduces the ClusterRole''s scope for defense in depth, complementing\nthe automountServiceAccountToken: false already in the pod spec.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): add RBAC safety guard verification to lint-chart job (#95)\n\nAdds a CI step that asserts helm template fails when\nbff.serviceAccount.create=false and bff.rbac.create=true without a\nnamed SA. This prevents regressions that remove the ClusterRoleBinding\nfail guard from passing CI undetected.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be992487c530582501e5be3faa1789eee16362da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/be992487c530582501e5be3faa1789eee16362da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/2073726c17ace08c4c332e34d8955ca1c5601878","verification":{"payload":"tree be992487c530582501e5be3faa1789eee16362da\nparent 62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28\nparent 1bd202d4d9563e299b3e80b0b65bcf0e29708f62\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784310668 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784310668 -0400\n\nfeat: Phase 7 — Helm Chart & Deployment Updates (#85)\n\n* feat(chart): add RBAC, configurable values, and CI/CD updates for Phase 7\n\n- Add ClusterRole and ClusterRoleBinding for BFF ServiceAccount with\n  permissions to manage plugin lifecycle operations (dashboard config\n  patching, namespace management, Helm-deployed resources)\n- Add bffServiceAccountName helper to _helpers.tpl\n- Expose charter registry URL, cache TTLs, and fetch concurrency as\n  configurable Helm values with env var injection in BFF deployment\n- Add bff.rbac.create toggle (default: true)\n- Update plugin.yaml rbac section with required cluster role declarations\n- Add Helm chart linting job to CI workflow\n- Add dev branch to CI triggers\n- Update OPENSHIFT_DEPLOY.md with RBAC documentation and new Helm values\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Always set serviceAccountName on BFF deployment (fixes pre-existing SA\n  pattern where create=false + name=my-sa silently fell back to default)\n- Remove redundant secrets rule from ClusterRole (already covered by core\n  resources rule)\n- Scope RBAC to namespace-scoped roles/rolebindings only instead of\n  cluster-scoped (prevents privilege escalation via ClusterRole creation)\n- Consolidate overlapping deployments rules into single rule\n- Sync plugin.yaml RBAC declarations with actual ClusterRole rules\n- Update deployment docs RBAC table to match\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Add template guard preventing ClusterRole binding to the ''default''\n  ServiceAccount — helm template now fails with a clear message when\n  bff.rbac.create=true but no SA is configured\n- Add bff.serviceAccount.name to Helm Chart Reference table in docs\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): disable SA token auto-mount in BFF pod spec (#91)\n\nThe BFF never reads the SA token — all Kubernetes API calls and Helm\noperations use the end user''s forwarded Bearer token. Setting\nautomountServiceAccountToken: false on the pod spec removes the\nunnecessarily mounted token and reduces the attack surface.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): add update/patch verbs to ClusterRole namespace rule (#92)\n\nThe namespaces rule was missing update and patch verbs, which are\nrequired when a community plugin''s Helm chart includes a Namespace\nresource directly. Without these verbs, helm upgrade would fail with\n403 Forbidden when reconciling changes on namespace objects.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): check source values instead of resolved name in RBAC fail guard (#93)\n\nReplaces the resolved-name check (`eq $saName \"default\"`) with a\nsource-values check so that explicitly naming a ServiceAccount \"default\"\nwith `bff.serviceAccount.create=true` is no longer incorrectly blocked.\nThe dangerous case — `bff.serviceAccount.create=false` with no name set —\nstill fails as expected.\n\nFixes #90\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): separate secrets into own ClusterRole rule without watch verb (#94)\n\nSplits secrets out of the bundled core resources rule and removes the\nwatch verb, which is not needed for Helm lifecycle operations. This\nreduces the ClusterRole''s scope for defense in depth, complementing\nthe automountServiceAccountToken: false already in the pod spec.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): add RBAC safety guard verification to lint-chart job (#95)\n\nAdds a CI step that asserts helm template fails when\nbff.serviceAccount.create=false and bff.rbac.create=true without a\nnamed SA. This prevents regressions that remove the ClusterRoleBinding\nfail guard from passing CI undetected.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWmuMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqRIQAFYIR7lQNbXdurwQFv1Yynzo\nxwjoe4SrowWeDOCgjETDo6WauiJI5ochGBEFJXIV/RNIiehXguuQ/x6/