ithub.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/9644c9af4c03567fe20ad0008e2ecc56b423145d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:55:47Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:55:47Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Always set serviceAccountName on BFF deployment (fixes pre-existing SA\n  pattern where create=false + name=my-sa silently fell back to default)\n- Remove redundant secrets rule from ClusterRole (already covered by core\n  resources rule)\n- Scope RBAC to namespace-scoped roles/rolebindings only instead of\n  cluster-scoped (prevents privilege escalation via ClusterRole creation)\n- Consolidate overlapping deployments rules into single rule\n- Sync plugin.yaml RBAC declarations with actual ClusterRole rules\n- Update deployment docs RBAC table to match\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"04467309a96ae1b31822ae44444b1b0a32555951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/04467309a96ae1b31822ae44444b1b0a32555951"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/9644c9af4c03567fe20ad0008e2ecc56b423145d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/9644c9af4c03567fe20ad0008e2ecc56b423145d","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKDk2NDRjOWFmNGMwMzU2N2ZlMjBhZDAwMDhlMmVjYzU2YjQyMzE0NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/4dacce82520176eb0b816f6cdd32bb39fd875572","sha":"4dacce82520176eb0b816f6cdd32bb39fd875572","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/4dacce82520176eb0b816f6cdd32bb39fd875572"}],"sha":"9644c9af4c03567fe20ad0008e2ecc56b423145d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/9644c9af4c03567fe20ad0008e2ecc56b423145d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/4dacce82520176eb0b816f6cdd32bb39fd875572/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:51:35Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:51:35Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"feat(chart): add RBAC, configurable values, and CI/CD updates for Phase 7\n\n- Add ClusterRole and ClusterRoleBinding for BFF ServiceAccount with\n  permissions to manage plugin lifecycle operations (dashboard config\n  patching, namespace management, Helm-deployed resources)\n- Add bffServiceAccountName helper to _helpers.tpl\n- Expose charter registry URL, cache TTLs, and fetch concurrency as\n  configurable Helm values with env var injection in BFF deployment\n- Add bff.rbac.create toggle (default: true)\n- Update plugin.yaml rbac section with required cluster role declarations\n- Add Helm chart linting job to CI workflow\n- Add dev branch to CI triggers\n- Update OPENSHIFT_DEPLOY.md with RBAC documentation and new Helm values\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"facdaa0fb262811b73c0a324a27840ef4bb631a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/facdaa0fb262811b73c0a324a27840ef4bb631a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/4dacce82520176eb0b816f6cdd32bb39fd875572","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/4dacce82520176eb0b816f6cdd32bb39fd875572","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKDRkYWNjZTgyNTIwMTc2ZWIwYjgxNmY2Y2RkMzJiYjM5ZmQ4NzU1NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28","sha":"62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28"}],"sha":"4dacce82520176eb0b816f6cdd32bb39fd875572","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/4dacce82520176eb0b816f6cdd32bb39fd875572"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:44:23Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:44:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 6 — Plugin Install / Upgrade / Remove (#65)\n\n* feat(bff): add plugin lifecycle endpoints and services\n\nAdd the BFF backend for plugin install/upgrade/remove/enable/disable:\n- K8s API client using the user''s forwarded Bearer token\n- Dashboard config service to read/modify MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG\n- Helm service executing Helm CLI with --kube-token for user auth\n- Lifecycle orchestration service coordinating multi-step flows\n- Express routes: POST install, POST upgrade, DELETE remove,\n  POST enable, POST disable at /api/plugins/:name/*\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(frontend): add plugin lifecycle UI with install/upgrade/remove/enable/disable\n\n- usePluginLifecycle hook for mutation operations against BFF\n- ConfirmRemoveModal requiring name re-typing before removal\n- LifecycleProgressModal with step-by-step progress display\n- PluginDetailModal action buttons now wired to lifecycle hooks\n  (automatic/assisted install, upgrade, disable, remove)\n- InstalledPage table actions wired for upgrade, disable, remove\n- Both pages refetch data on lifecycle completion\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add Helm binary to BFF container and BFF ServiceAccount to chart\n\n- BFF Containerfile: multi-stage Helm install from official tarball\n- Helm chart: bff-serviceaccount.yaml template, deployment uses SA\n- values.yaml: bff.serviceAccount.create toggle\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add remote/federation config fields to PluginMetadata type\n\nAdd the remote block (type, spec with name/scope/remoteEntry/paths)\nto both BFF PluginMetadata and frontend CatalogPlugin types.\nThe lifecycle service now uses remote.spec.scope from plugin metadata\nwhen constructing MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG entries.\n\nCloses #7\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove unused onEnable prop from PluginDetailContent\n\nEnable button deferred until deployed-but-disabled state detection\nis implemented. The enable lifecycle action remains available in the\nhook for future use.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: update PluginDetailModal tests for active lifecycle buttons\n\nAction buttons are no longer aria-disabled stubs — they are now\nfully wired to lifecycle hooks. Updated tests to mock\nusePluginLifecycle and verify buttons are enabled and clickable.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add unit tests for plugin lifecycle features\n\nBFF tests:\n- dashboardConfigService: scope conversion, config read/write, patch\n- helmService: install/upgrade/uninstall with user token forwarding\n- lifecycleRoute: auth, validation, and success for all 5 endpoints\n\nFrontend tests:\n- usePluginLifecycle: all mutation functions, state management, reset\n- ConfirmRemoveModal: name matching, disable/enable, callbacks\n- LifecycleProgressModal: step rendering, success/error states\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\nSecurity and code quality fixes from cross-model review:\n\n- Validate Helm --set keys/values against allowlist patterns (HIGH)\n- Validate namespace parameter format and reject protected namespaces (HIGH)\n- Sanitize --kube-token from Helm error messages to prevent token leakage (MEDIUM)\n- Default rejectUnauthorized=true for K8s API TLS, require explicit opt-out (MEDIUM)\n- Add explicit body size limit (100kb) to Express JSON parser (MEDIUM)\n- Add content-type check before parsing JSON in frontend lifecycle hook (MEDIUM)\n- Reset confirm text when pluginName changes in ConfirmRemoveModal (MEDIUM)\n- Add isSafeUrl guard to manual install instructions URL (LOW)\n- Replace dynamic import with static import in lifecycleService (LOW)\n- Show \"Plugin not found\" instead of spinner for missing plugin state (LOW)\n- Remove sensitive error details from lifecycle route catch blocks (MEDIUM)\n- Hardcode Helm binary path instead of allowing env var override (LOW)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Fix scopeToKebab leading hyphen for PascalCase inputs (MEDIUM)\n- Remove redundant getModuleFederationConfig pre-check in disablePlugin (MEDIUM)\n- Find dashboard container by name instead of hardcoding index 0 (MEDIUM)\n- Sanitize internal cluster details from LifecycleResponse error messages (MEDIUM)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lifecycle): resolve recursive self-call in sanitizeErrorMessage (#73)\n\nReplace the unconditional self-call `const raw = sanitizeErrorMessage(err)`\n(which caused RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded on every lifecycle\nerror) with the correct base-case extraction:\n  const raw = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\n\nExport the function and add unit tests covering: no-infinite-recursion guard,\nError vs non-Error inputs, and all three redaction patterns (kube-token,\nservice-account, api-server IP:port).\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(k8s): use three-state sentinel for CA cert negative caching (#74)\n\nIntroduce a Buffer | null | undefined sentinel for cachedCaCert so that\na missing CA cert file (null) is distinguishable from the \"not yet\nchecked\" initial state (undefined). Previously the catch block reset\ncachedCaCert to undefined, causing fs.readFileSync to fire on every k8s\nrequest when running outside a pod.\n\nAlso exports getCaCert and adds unit tests covering both the positive\ncache (cert file present) and negative cache (cert file absent) paths.\n\nFixes #70\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(containerfile): add SHA256 checksum verification for Helm binary (#75)\n\nPin and verify the SHA256 checksum of the Helm v3.17.3 linux-amd64 tarball\nduring the container build. The tarball is now downloaded to a temp file,\nverified with sha256sum (failing the build on mismatch), then extracted and\ncleaned up — replacing the previous pipe-to-tar approach that skipped verification.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(detail-modal): show disabled install button when plugin has no install config (#76)\n\nWhen plugin.install is undefined, render an aria-disabled Install button\nwrapped in a Tooltip explaining that install configuration is not available,\nso admins see an informative state instead of an empty footer.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(helm): pass token via kubeconfig file instead of CLI argument (#77)\n\nWrite the bearer token to a per-invocation temporary kubeconfig file\n(mode 0o600) and pass --kubeconfig instead of --kube-token so the token\nis never visible in /proc/<pid>/cmdline. Also scopes HELM_CACHE_HOME,\nHELM_CONFIG_HOME, and HELM_DATA_HOME to per-invocation subdirs of the\ntemp directory to prevent concurrent-operation conflicts. The temp\ndirectory is removed in a finally block on both success and failure.\n\nFixes #64\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): look up actual scope from stored config instead of re-deriving (#78)\n\nremovePluginFromConfig previously called kebabToCamelScope(pluginName) to\nderive the scope, which always yields lowerCamelCase. When a plugin is added\nvia addPluginToConfig the scope comes verbatim from plugin.yaml\n(e.g. \"CommunityPluginsAdmin\", PascalCase), so the derived scope never\nmatched and the function threw \"Plugin not found in MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG\".\n\nFix: find the stored entry by round-tripping each scope through scopeToKebab\nand comparing to the plugin name. This correctly matches any case variant\n(camelCase, PascalCase, etc.) stored at install time.\n\nCloses #67\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lifecycle): track install namespace for upgrade and remove operations (#79)\n\nAdd discoverReleaseNamespace() to helmService that uses\n`helm list --all-namespaces --filter <name> --output json` to look up\nthe namespace of an existing Helm release by its exact name.\n\nupgradePlugin and removePlugin now accept an optional namespace parameter.\nWhen omitted, they call discoverReleaseNamespace and fall back to the\nplugin name only if the release cannot be found. The correct namespace is\nused for both the Helm operation and namespace deletion (deleteNamespace=true).\n\nThe upgrade and remove route handlers validate and pass through the\noptional namespace body field (POST /upgrade) and query param (DELETE /:name).\n\nCloses #62\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): add Enable button for disabled plugins on catalog page (#80)\n\n* fix(ui): add Enable button for disabled plugins on catalog page\n\nCloses #69. After disabling a plugin its Helm release still exists but it\nis removed from MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG, making it invisible to the admin\nwith no way to re-enable it.\n\n- BFF: add `helmListAllNamespaces()` to helmService and expose it via a new\n  `GET /api/plugins` endpoint that returns all installed Helm releases\n- Frontend: add `useHelmReleasedPlugins` hook that fetches that endpoint to\n  build a set of Helm-installed plugin names\n- CatalogPage: block on Helm data load alongside MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG;\n  show an orange \"Disabled\" badge on cards for plugins that are Helm-installed\n  but not in MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG; add \"Disabled\" to the install-state\n  filter options; wire Refresh to also refetch Helm and installed-names data;\n  pass `helmInstalledNames` to PluginDetailModal\n- PluginDetailModal: accept optional `helmInstalledNames` prop; derive\n  `disabled = helmInstalled && !enabled`; show \"Disabled\" badge in the modal\n  header; replace install buttons with Enable + Remove buttons for disabled\n  plugins; add `onEnable` handler that calls `lifecycle.enable()`\n- Fix pre-existing BFF test compilation error: add js-yaml type stub and\n  fix helmService partial mock so validateHelmValues keeps its real impl\n- Tests: new useHelmReleasedPlugins hook tests; new CatalogPage Disabled-badge\n  tests; new PluginDetailModal disabled-state tests; new GET /api/plugins\n  route tests; helmListAllNamespaces unit tests\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\n- Remove internal try/catch from helmListAllNamespaces so errors propagate to the route handler''s catch block\n- Update helmService tests to expect thrown errors instead of empty arrays\n- Add blank line between router.get(''/'') closing brace and K8S_NAMESPACE_PATTERN constant\n- Remove multi-line JSDoc comment from useHelmReleasedPlugins\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): handle missing env array in JSON Patch for first plugin install (#81)\n\nWhen a dashboard container has no env field at all, using op:''add'' with\npath ending in /env/- violates RFC 6902 §4.1 (append to existing array)\nand the Kubernetes API rejects it with HTTP 422.  Detect whether the\ntarget container already has an env array and use env (without /-) to\ncreate it on first install, falling back to env/- for subsequent patches.\n\nAdds two test cases to dashboardConfigService.test.ts:\n- appends via env/- when container already has an env array\n- creates env array via env (no /-) when container has no env field\n\nFixes #68\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(catalog): show version comparison on catalog cards for installed plugins (#82)\n\nExtends the HelmRelease interface (BFF and frontend) to include\napp_version from helm list output. The hook now exposes a helmVersionMap\n(Map<name, installedVersion>) alongside helmInstalledNames. Catalog cards\ncompare the installed version against the catalog version and display a\n''Update available: X → Y'' label (PatternFly blue Label with\nArrowCircleUpIcon) when they differ; no indicator is shown when versions\nmatch or when version info is unavailable.\n\nCloses #21\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lifecycle): share single usePluginLifecycle instance between page and modal (#83)\n\nInstalledPage and PluginDetailModal previously each called usePluginLifecycle()\nindependently, allowing concurrent lifecycle operations to race against the same\nbackend state with no coordination.\n\n- Export PluginLifecycleState and PluginLifecycle types from the hook module\n- Add lifecycle prop (required) to PluginDetailModalProps; remove the internal\n  usePluginLifecycle() call from PluginDetailModal\n- Pass the page-level lifecycle instance to PluginDetailModal from InstalledPage\n- Create and pass a lifecycle instance from CatalogPage to PluginDetailModal\n- Disable row-level Upgrade, Disable, and Remove actions in InstalledPage while\n  lifecycle.loading is true, so both the table and the open modal reflect the\n  same in-progress state\n- Update PluginDetailModal tests to pass lifecycle as a prop instead of mocking\n  the hook\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): add optimistic concurrency control for MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG updates (#84)\n\nRead the deployment resourceVersion on every attempt and prepend a JSON Patch\ntest operation that verifies it before applying the mutation. Kubernetes rejects\nthe patch with HTTP 409 if the resource was modified concurrently. Both\naddPluginToConfig and removePluginFromConfig are wrapped in withRetryOnConflict,\nwhich re-reads the latest deployment state and retries up to 3 times on 409.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"626664c6a6f8eb3e74af6699fc4f18f759d23e8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/626664c6a6f8eb3e74af6699fc4f18f759d23e8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28","verification":{"payload":"tree 626664c6a6f8eb3e74af6699fc4f18f759d23e8e\nparent e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33\nparent dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784303063 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784303063 -0400\n\nfeat: Phase 6 — Plugin Install / Upgrade / Remove (#65)\n\n* feat(bff): add plugin lifecycle endpoints and services\n\nAdd the BFF backend for plugin install/upgrade/remove/enable/disable:\n- K8s API client using the user''s forwarded Bearer token\n- Dashboard config service to read/modify MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG\n- Helm service executing Helm CLI with --kube-token for user auth\n- Lifecycle orchestration service coordinating multi-step flows\n- Express routes: POST install, POST upgrade, DELETE remove,\n  POST enable, POST disable at /api/plugins/:name/*\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(frontend): add plugin lifecycle UI with install/upgrade/remove/enable/disable\n\n- usePluginLifecycle hook for mutation operations against BFF\n- ConfirmRemoveModal requiring name re-typing before removal\n- LifecycleProgressModal with step-by-step progress display\n- PluginDetailModal action buttons now wired to lifecycle hooks\n  (automatic/assisted install, upgrade, disable, remove)\n- InstalledPage table actions wired for upgrade, disable, remove\n- Both pages refetch data on lifecycle completion\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add Helm binary to BFF container and BFF ServiceAccount to chart\n\n- BFF Containerfile: multi-stage Helm install from official tarball\n- Helm chart: bff-serviceaccount.yaml template, deployment uses SA\n- values.yaml: bff.serviceAccount.create toggle\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add remote/federation config fields to PluginMetadata type\n\nAdd the remote block (type, spec with name/scope/remoteEntry/paths)\nto both BFF PluginMetadata and frontend CatalogPlugin types.\nThe lifecycle service now uses remote.spec.scope from plugin metadata\nwhen constructing MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG entries.\n\nCloses #7\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove unused onEnable prop from PluginDetailContent\n\nEnable button deferred until deployed-but-disabled state detection\nis implemented. The enable lifecycle action remains available in the\nhook for future use.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: update PluginDetailModal tests for active lifecycle buttons\n\nAction buttons are no longer aria-disabled stubs — they are now\nfully wired to lifecycle hooks. Updated tests to mock\nusePluginLifecycle and verify buttons are enabled and clickable.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add unit tests for plugin lifecycle features\n\nBFF tests:\n- dashboardConfigService: scope conversion, config read/write, patch\n- helmService: install/upgrade/uninstall with user token forwarding\n- lifecycleRoute: auth, validation, and success for all 5 endpoints\n\nFrontend tests:\n- usePluginLifecycle: all mutation functions, state management, reset\n- ConfirmRemoveModal: name matching, disable/enable, callbacks\n- LifecycleProgressModal: step rendering, success/error states\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\nSecurity and code quality fixes from cross-model review:\n\n- Validate Helm --set keys/values against allowlist patterns (HIGH)\n- Validate namespace parameter format and reject protected namespaces (HIGH)\n- Sanitize --kube-token from Helm error messages to prevent token leakage (MEDIUM)\n- Default rejectUnauthorized=true for K8s API TLS, require explicit opt-out (MEDIUM)\n- Add explicit body size limit (100kb) to Express JSON parser (MEDIUM)\n- Add content-type check before parsing JSON in frontend lifecycle hook (MEDIUM)\n- Reset confirm text when pluginName changes in ConfirmRemoveModal (MEDIUM)\n- Add isSafeUrl guard to manual install instructions URL (LOW)\n- Replace dynamic import with static import in lifecycleService (LOW)\n- Show \"Plugin not found\" instead of spinner for missing plugin state (LOW)\n- Remove sensitive error details from lifecycle route catch blocks (MEDIUM)\n- Hardcode Helm binary path instead of allowing env var override (LOW)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 2)\n\n- Fix scopeToKebab leading hyphen for PascalCase inputs (MEDIUM)\n- Remove redundant getModuleFederationConfig pre-check in disablePlugin (MEDIUM)\n- Find dashboard container by name instead of hardcoding index 0 (MEDIUM)\n- Sanitize internal cluster details from LifecycleResponse error messages (MEDIUM)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lifecycle): resolve recursive self-call in sanitizeErrorMessage (#73)\n\nReplace the unconditional self-call `const raw = sanitizeErrorMessage(err)`\n(which caused RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded on every lifecycle\nerror) with the correct base-case extraction:\n  const raw = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\n\nExport the function and add unit tests covering: no-infinite-recursion guard,\nError vs non-Error inputs, and all three redaction patterns (kube-token,\nservice-account, api-server IP:port).\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(k8s): use three-state sentinel for CA cert negative caching (#74)\n\nIntroduce a Buffer | null | undefined sentinel for cachedCaCert so that\na missing CA cert file (null) is distinguishable from the \"not yet\nchecked\" initial state (undefined). Previously the catch block reset\ncachedCaCert to undefined, causing fs.readFileSync to fire on every k8s\nrequest when running outside a pod.\n\nAlso exports getCaCert and adds unit tests covering both the positive\ncache (cert file present) and negative cache (cert file absent) paths.\n\nFixes #70\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(containerfile): add SHA256 checksum verification for Helm binary (#75)\n\nPin and verify the SHA256 checksum of the Helm v3.17.3 linux-amd64 tarball\nduring the container build. The tarball is now downloaded to a temp file,\nverified with sha256sum (failing the build on mismatch), then extracted and\ncleaned up — replacing the previous pipe-to-tar approach that skipped verification.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(detail-modal): show disabled install button when plugin has no install config (#76)\n\nWhen plugin.install is undefined, render an aria-disabled Install button\nwrapped in a Tooltip explaining that install configuration is not available,\nso admins see an informative state instead of an empty footer.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(helm): pass token via kubeconfig file instead of CLI argument (#77)\n\nWrite the bearer token to a per-invocation temporary kubeconfig file\n(mode 0o600) and pass --kubeconfig instead of --kube-token so the token\nis never visible in /proc/<pid>/cmdline. Also scopes HELM_CACHE_HOME,\nHELM_CONFIG_HOME, and HELM_DATA_HOME to per-invocation subdirs of the\ntemp directory to prevent concurrent-operation conflicts. The temp\ndirectory is removed in a finally block on both success and failure.\n\nFixes #64\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): look up actual scope from stored config instead of re-deriving (#78)\n\nremovePluginFromConfig previously called kebabToCamelScope(pluginName) to\nderive the scope, which always yields lowerCamelCase. When a plugin is added\nvia addPluginToConfig the scope comes verbatim from plugin.yaml\n(e.g. \"CommunityPluginsAdmin\", PascalCase), so the derived scope never\nmatched and the function threw \"Plugin not found in MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG\".\n\nFix: find the stored entry by round-tripping each scope through scopeToKebab\nand comparing to the plugin name. This correctly matches any case variant\n(camelCase, PascalCase, etc.) stored at install time.\n\nCloses #67\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lifecycle): track install namespace for upgrade and remove operations (#79)\n\nAdd discoverReleaseNamespace() to helmService that uses\n`helm list --all-namespaces --filter <name> --output json` to look up\nthe namespace of an existing Helm release by its exact name.\n\nupgradePlugin and removePlugin now accept an optional namespace parameter.\nWhen omitted, they call discoverReleaseNamespace and fall back to the\nplugin name only if the release cannot be found. The correct namespace is\nused for both the Helm operation and namespace deletion (deleteNamespace=true).\n\nThe upgrade and remove route handlers validate and pass through the\noptional namespace body field (POST /upgrade) and query param (DELETE /:name).\n\nCloses #62\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): add Enable button for disabled plugins on catalog page (#80)\n\n* fix(ui): add Enable button for disabled plugins on catalog page\n\nCloses #69. After disabling a plugin its Helm release still exists but it\nis removed from MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG, making it invisible to the admin\nwith no way to re-enable it.\n\n- BFF: add `helmListAllNamespaces()` to helmService and expose it via a new\n  `GET /api/plugins` endpoint that returns all installed Helm releases\n- Frontend: add `useHelmReleasedPlugins` hook that fetches that endpoint to\n  build a set of Helm-installed plugin names\n- CatalogPage: block on Helm data load alongside MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG;\n  show an orange \"Disabled\" badge on cards for plugins that are Helm-installed\n  but not in MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG; add \"Disabled\" to the install-state\n  filter options; wire Refresh to also refetch Helm and installed-names data;\n  pass `helmInstalledNames` to PluginDetailModal\n- PluginDetailModal: accept optional `helmInstalledNames` prop; derive\n  `disabled = helmInstalled && !enabled`; show \"Disabled\" badge in the modal\n  header; replace install buttons with Enable + Remove buttons for disabled\n  plugins; add `onEnable` handler that calls `lifecycle.enable()`\n- Fix pre-existing BFF test compilation error: add js-yaml type stub and\n  fix helmService partial mock so validateHelmValues keeps its real impl\n- Tests: new useHelmReleasedPlugins hook tests; new CatalogPage Disabled-badge\n  tests; new PluginDetailModal disabled-state tests; new GET /api/plugins\n  route tests; helmListAllNamespaces unit tests\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (round 1)\n\n- Remove internal try/catch from helmListAllNamespaces so errors propagate to the route handler''s catch block\n- Update helmService tests to expect thrown errors instead of empty arrays\n- Add blank line between router.get(''/'') closing brace and K8S_NAMESPACE_PATTERN constant\n- Remove multi-line JSDoc comment from useHelmReleasedPlugins\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): handle missing env array in JSON Patch for first plugin install (#81)\n\nWhen a dashboard container has no env field at all, using op:''add'' with\npath ending in /env/- violates RFC 6902 §4.1 (append to existing array)\nand the Kubernetes API rejects it with HTTP 422.  Detect whether the\ntarget container already has an env array and use env (without /-) to\ncreate it on first install, falling back to env/- for subsequent patches.\n\nAdds two test cases to dashboardConfigService.test.ts:\n- appends via env/- when container already has an env array\n- creates env array via env (no /-) when container has no env field\n\nFixes #68\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(catalog): show version comparison on catalog cards for installed plugins (#82)\n\nExtends the HelmRelease interface (BFF and frontend) to include\napp_version from helm list output. The hook now exposes a helmVersionMap\n(Map<name, installedVersion>) alongside helmInstalledNames. Catalog cards\ncompare the installed version against the catalog version and display a\n''Update available: X → Y'' label (PatternFly blue Label with\nArrowCircleUpIcon) when they differ; no indicator is shown when versions\nmatch or when version info is unavailable.\n\nCloses #21\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(lifecycle): share single usePluginLifecycle instance between page and modal (#83)\n\nInstalledPage and PluginDetailModal previously each called usePluginLifecycle()\nindependently, allowing concurrent lifecycle operations to race against the same\nbackend state with no coordination.\n\n- Export PluginLifecycleState and PluginLifecycle types from the hook module\n- Add lifecycle prop (required) to PluginDetailModalProps; remove the internal\n  usePluginLifecycle() call from PluginDetailModal\n- Pass the page-level lifecycle instance to PluginDetailModal from InstalledPage\n- Create and pass a lifecycle instance from CatalogPage to PluginDetailModal\n- Disable row-level Upgrade, Disable, and Remove actions in InstalledPage while\n  lifecycle.loading is true, so both the table and the open modal reflect the\n  same in-progress state\n- Update PluginDetailModal tests to pass lifecycle as a prop instead of mocking\n  the hook\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): add optimistic concurrency control for MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG updates (#84)\n\nRead the deployment resourceVersion on every attempt and prepend a JSON Patch\ntest operation that verifies it before applying the mutation. Kubernetes rejects\nthe patch with HTTP 409 if the resource was modified concurrently. Both\naddPluginToConfig and removePluginFromConfig are wrapped in withRetryOnConflict,\nwhich re-reads the latest deployment state and retries up to 3 times on 409.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWk3XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATKYQAHCOVQHjZj0RF512ygGr56DS\nU6Mw48daquC0jtkhHUI5Y5SD58r/1sJP8/3jyDheJ+a5+oKSu3Ep3KPYVEbMlJpf\n8mLThuTHN55ggeu/LBjxHltHlOhDoKP7gH9uCuJ8toyo3kQlViJqEWfZimbP5DYp\nUhuk/OIgQfCkF8v/YGRxpZy6TuNaPDPgrffY1gg+UqrVgNBoIWPWEgx0H4vz063l\nmbcex6fwbeb2ISPIxOlGJI2mxxrXnWCZGzA9U524pARacA+FbecITqRPTyK5LlRy\nCcd58d3a6OglcjqhrN28nhTO5NUnRq+8vmO+tGER7cEKkpJjrEEId3GGP170W9C6\nx4j3WPDP8bGv+D5Kz+OT8vFbCHV2kWIIPqaZ3lDWg/iVtRtfvmBcy9NoP7lPkytG\nq52F4BU1qtOFpZgGxODu2aPhKKyrS2wSJr5ELPV9suY4N71kVn6z+NoO5i/HZRGN\n3PXyWbvX9TPpB34wKdhMwWZUee8GRgh/RfDWNPjxGQOJESnMkdzKivzXOd/Xt2YI\nSRgONef5hBa2twwUoep2GRfJ+n3kRILzRts95mBk5VZILqadqbW9wWrDZKx2i/0/\nk79ZkStyTxBMR58JewBFk+A/qYdjOZ9Kt8Bb27X9xZNtOa4gjmufkspYC32EfTeC\neO5bbf6qMXCKa6GVyuMv\n=h1/z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T15:44:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKDYyYmFlMGRiODM0ZjhkMDg4YTUwNjg2NmFlMmYxMGYxYmUxYWNkMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33","sha":"e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8","sha":"dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8"}],"sha":"62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/62bae0db834f8d088a506866ae2f10f1be1acd28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:40:09Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:40:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(config): add optimistic concurrency control for MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG updates (#84)\n\nRead the deployment resourceVersion on every attempt and prepend a JSON Patch\ntest operation that verifies it before applying the mutation. Kubernetes rejects\nthe patch with HTTP 409 if the resource was modified concurrently. Both\naddPluginToConfig and removePluginFromConfig are wrapped in withRetryOnConflict,\nwhich re-reads the latest deployment state and retries up to 3 times on 409.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"626664c6a6f8eb3e74af6699fc4f18f759d23e8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/626664c6a6f8eb3e74af6699fc4f18f759d23e8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8","verification":{"payload":"tree 626664c6a6f8eb3e74af6699fc4f18f759d23e8e\nparent 163cdfebadd11108f439dcaf5ca82b22e6e1b6a6\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784302809 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784302809 -0400\n\nfix(config): add optimistic concurrency control for MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG updates (#84)\n\nRead the deployment resourceVersion on every attempt and prepend a JSON Patch\ntest operation that verifies it before applying the mutation. Kubernetes rejects\nthe patch with HTTP 409 if the resource was modified concurrently. Both\naddPluginToConfig and removePluginFromConfig are wrapped in withRetryOnConflict,\nwhich re-reads the latest deployment state and retries up to 3 times on 409.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWkzZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABc0QAAbQ8BEeLG8lfk9rKroZBdfs\nLhPuXbaHmO++LewCFSsfzXUdBSqYNrBTptTncDyAjCoHTPbnVWY8M0GwgiDMjjzb\nUIt0+TGSZah7rorsHp415OWgymOxq7ZFvj+Qxnh/DBGDbP1Kn9zaweXYEtdXDIdF\nbk3lYOyBcvo/HVejC2WTcP5mH0SgsiHZ6pH6qElzRhXx5NndJK3zRCogsDT0tYD2\nYouOum97yv3x3Aqw83HajLcSMXM0uDyh4zB9rdyNBNUj9QuE6EWhrI/IUmtEPKLh\nfOeqntbX6/vg8anZgqV92Yt5mmblP7a7Fup4KER4Yxvv4KKj10oyp/O1t40lXLbz\nj6PajIXCN9yK380H34g2dxbWqAkEDNXmFoj7cWVr+WnPHYVCVTV60ZRkpvyzo7E6\nH1tFXjPY0IERzOLT9XAj5fOzfj2dPfLkK04TFq3TCs38zSb/c53eBLhiCeUzbYnC\nwwIgFqkdR6lu03BpB3CN9xJLnVvNqbanmZLjg/CWkxujNrNmSfHBcYdI37bvHZ2X\neg7bYrzZ9PWorm5DONJ/9Cmj9SWjqC13A19pn4tJrYIn+I5YfZ+4sVabRBX2/FQH\nUIsJfwqgEvlwh3RKgum59+e1uYfL9UwfOWRvkeelUCJdlRTmvWN3xzdB9veihpP8\nqp6Flz7JcPFq6UC48hxg\n=UAff\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T15:40:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKGRlYTYxNmJhN2U5NDg3YTFjZWMzNjNkMmNmNjM3NDgyN2ZlMjZiYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/163cdfebadd11108f439dcaf5ca82b22e6e1b6a6","sha":"163cdfebadd11108f439dcaf5ca82b22e6e1b6a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/163cdfebadd11108f439dcaf5ca82b22e6e1b6a6"}],"sha":"dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/dea616ba7e9487a1cec363d2cf6374827fe26bc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/163cdfebadd11108f439dcaf5ca82b22e6e1b6a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:28:46Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T15:28:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(lifecycle): share single usePluginLifecycle instance between page and modal (#83)\n\nInstalledPage and PluginDetailModal previously each called usePluginLifecycle()\nindependently, allowing concurrent lifecycle operations to race against the same\nbackend state with no coordination.\n\n- Export PluginLifecycleState and PluginLifecycle types from the hook module\n- Add lifecycle prop (required) to PluginDetailModalProps; remove the internal\n  usePluginLifecycle() call from PluginDetailModal\n- Pass the page-level lifecycle instance to PluginDetailModal from InstalledPage\n- Create and pass a lifecycle instance from CatalogPage to PluginDetailModal\n- Disable row-level Upgrade, Disable, and Remove actions in InstalledPage while\n  lifecycle.loading is true, so both the table and the open modal reflect the\n  same in-progress state\n- Update PluginDetailModal tests to pass lifecycle as a prop instead of mocking\n  the hook\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be1edd3c9806d84aaba24d283bbaacc10442635c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/be1edd3c9806d84aaba24d283bbaacc10442635c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/163cdfebadd11108f439dcaf5ca82b22e6e1b6a6","verification":{"payload":"tree be1edd3c9806d84aaba24d283bbaacc10442635c\nparent 01b5de7ccfc60f6c3de244535409ec659d476442\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784302126 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784302126 -0400\n\nfix(lifecycle): share single usePluginLifecycle instance between page and modal (#83)\n\nInstalledPage and PluginDetailModal previously each called usePluginLifecycle()\nindependently, allowing concurrent lifecycle operations to race against the same\nbackend state with no coordination.\n\n- Export PluginLifecycleState and PluginLifecycle types from the hook module\n- Add lifecycle prop (required) to PluginDetailModalProps; remove the internal\n  usePluginLifecycle() call from PluginDetailModal\n- Pass the page-level lifecycle instance to PluginDetailModal from InstalledPage\n- Create and pass a lifecycle instance from CatalogPage to PluginDetailModal\n- Disable row-level Upgrade, Disable, and Remove actions in InstalledPage while\n  lifecycle.loading is true, so both the table and the open modal reflect the\n  same in-progress state\n- Update PluginDetailModal tests to pass lifecycle as a prop instead of mocking\n  the hook\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWkouCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr/oQADUO9QHmM0DPrT0GkRFnYXOs\nQnWA+gGYXyb6TYGxApjvVVPIoRSMQGWa7ycAGRkQHaDn0d2Gyb7d8y7DM2LQuBIf\nDP+OKSO5Ogb9ITvx6RsAwDlvLuzs78K6surGquQeZ9+ZJoYYcaGwNR9Z8YZeBuj4\n/QnwpqH2xRCjqKbYA9XriaeXsMQXmSmmA/5qSP6Wh3CIyMXqZDn8Kcc9eqgkn9j6\np0HN05KYOa+0BUkBGYWqKMZJ88OSbkxpJzQ++LBEtwqs/eLWRem3vdHtEVcgcD/h\ngquEnFlUpKKQTp4yG9wT0tZhMY+bW15hlgwYsAevNuTLnq5wD9bsR51XabHrMfxY\n44eNi+Hwuwh1ZiRI3QNzo7fYF6nH1cqiIR1bwX0anGSfzdYlJ9A0Q6sA1SLL+4SV\nIC+