tarred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/a31841ad4ae356dd721e3adefafc3973b3df255f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:01:33Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:01:33Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"feat(bff): add plugin lifecycle endpoints and services\n\nAdd the BFF backend for plugin install/upgrade/remove/enable/disable:\n- K8s API client using the user''s forwarded Bearer token\n- Dashboard config service to read/modify MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG\n- Helm service executing Helm CLI with --kube-token for user auth\n- Lifecycle orchestration service coordinating multi-step flows\n- Express routes: POST install, POST upgrade, DELETE remove,\n  POST enable, POST disable at /api/plugins/:name/*\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"05ae9db1f83de9e4eaec10438d1792b393820400","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/05ae9db1f83de9e4eaec10438d1792b393820400"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/a31841ad4ae356dd721e3adefafc3973b3df255f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/a31841ad4ae356dd721e3adefafc3973b3df255f","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKGEzMTg0MWFkNGFlMzU2ZGQ3MjFlM2FkZWZhZmMzOTczYjNkZjI1NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33","sha":"e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33"}],"sha":"a31841ad4ae356dd721e3adefafc3973b3df255f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/a31841ad4ae356dd721e3adefafc3973b3df255f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T13:52:06Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T13:52:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 5 — Plugin Detail Modal with full metadata and admin action stubs (#50)\n\n* feat: Phase 5 — Plugin Detail Modal with full metadata and admin action stubs\n\n- Create usePluginDetail hook that fetches GET /api/catalog/:name and\n  resolves installed state from useInstalledPluginNames\n- Rewrite PluginDetailModal from placeholder to full detail modal:\n  header with version/status/maintenance badges, description, maintainer,\n  RHOAI compatibility, deployment model, container images, install method\n  with prerequisites, RBAC requirements, and support links\n- Add admin-only action buttons (Install/Upgrade/Disable/Remove) as\n  aria-disabled stubs for Phase 6 implementation\n- Pass isAdmin prop from CatalogPage and InstalledPage to the modal\n- Add useCurrentUser to CatalogPage for admin detection\n- Add comprehensive tests for usePluginDetail hook (8 tests) and\n  PluginDetailModal component (17 tests)\n- Update CatalogPage and InstalledPage tests with modal mock\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Rename usePluginDetail.test.ts to .spec.ts to match Jest testMatch\n  pattern — tests were silently skipped\n- Add isSafeUrl guard on support link hrefs to prevent javascript: XSS\n- Extract shared statusLabelColor to ~/app/utils/maintenance.ts,\n  removing duplication between CatalogPage and PluginDetailModal\n- Reset plugin state to null before new fetch to prevent stale data\n- Move Close button outside isAdmin guard so non-admin users get a\n  footer Close button too\n- Remove no-op afterEach mockRestore in hook tests\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hooks): remove duplicate useInstalledPluginNames call from usePluginDetail (#56)\n\nAccept installedNames and installedLoading as parameters instead of\ncalling useInstalledPluginNames() internally. Parent pages already\nhave this data and now pass it through the modal props, eliminating\nduplicate K8s API requests on every page load.\n\nCloses #53\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(modal): prevent loading and error states from rendering simultaneously (#57)\n\nGuard error branch with !loading in PluginDetailModal and suppress\ncombined loading in usePluginDetail when an error is present. This\nprevents dual ModalHeader and overlapping spinner + error alert when\na fetch fails while installedLoading is still true.\n\nCloses #51\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(modal): show spinner instead of empty body on initial modal open (#58)\n\n* fix(modal): show spinner instead of empty body on initial modal open\n\nAdd fallback branch in PluginDetailModal for the transitional state\nwhere pluginName is set but useEffect has not yet fired (loading=false,\nplugin=null, error=null). This eliminates a one-frame empty modal body.\n\nCloses #52\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use consistent pluginName fallback in modal header\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): use consistent deployment model formatting across pages (#59)\n\nMove deploymentModelLabel to shared utils and use it in CatalogPage\ncard footer, matching the formatted display already used in\nPluginDetailModal (e.g., ''Cluster-shared'' instead of ''cluster-shared'').\n\nCloses #54\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(modal): guard container image rendering against missing fields (#60)\n\nAdd runtime guards for image.repository before rendering and fall\nback to ''latest'' when image.tag is absent. Prevents displaying\n''repository:undefined'' from malformed BFF responses.\n\nCloses #55\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3795058dc43a439bff039c8e8812b03ec2d6282b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/3795058dc43a439bff039c8e8812b03ec2d6282b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/e91c41e63af1c5e92c08e954d5e24ece9aeacb33","verification":{"payload":"tree 3795058dc43a439bff039c8e8812b03ec2d6282b\nparent fef8a37cfad8eb37fdb56452c95902c22dab6e96\nparent a429524dc36a49dc2406ef0f1c4cefb9c4defc01\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784296326 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784296326 -0400\n\nfeat: Phase 5 — Plugin Detail Modal with full metadata and admin action stubs (#50)\n\n* feat: Phase 5 — Plugin Detail Modal with full metadata and admin action stubs\n\n- Create usePluginDetail hook that fetches GET /api/catalog/:name and\n  resolves installed state from useInstalledPluginNames\n- Rewrite PluginDetailModal from placeholder to full detail modal:\n  header with version/status/maintenance badges, description, maintainer,\n  RHOAI compatibility, deployment model, container images, install method\n  with prerequisites, RBAC requirements, and support links\n- Add admin-only action buttons (Install/Upgrade/Disable/Remove) as\n  aria-disabled stubs for Phase 6 implementation\n- Pass isAdmin prop from CatalogPage and InstalledPage to the modal\n- Add useCurrentUser to CatalogPage for admin detection\n- Add comprehensive tests for usePluginDetail hook (8 tests) and\n  PluginDetailModal component (17 tests)\n- Update CatalogPage and InstalledPage tests with modal mock\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Rename usePluginDetail.test.ts to .spec.ts to match Jest testMatch\n  pattern — tests were silently skipped\n- Add isSafeUrl guard on support link hrefs to prevent javascript: XSS\n- Extract shared statusLabelColor to ~/app/utils/maintenance.ts,\n  removing duplication between CatalogPage and PluginDetailModal\n- Reset plugin state to null before new fetch to prevent stale data\n- Move Close button outside isAdmin guard so non-admin users get a\n  footer Close button too\n- Remove no-op afterEach mockRestore in hook tests\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hooks): remove duplicate useInstalledPluginNames call from usePluginDetail (#56)\n\nAccept installedNames and installedLoading as parameters instead of\ncalling useInstalledPluginNames() internally. Parent pages already\nhave this data and now pass it through the modal props, eliminating\nduplicate K8s API requests on every page load.\n\nCloses #53\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(modal): prevent loading and error states from rendering simultaneously (#57)\n\nGuard error branch with !loading in PluginDetailModal and suppress\ncombined loading in usePluginDetail when an error is present. This\nprevents dual ModalHeader and overlapping spinner + error alert when\na fetch fails while installedLoading is still true.\n\nCloses #51\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(modal): show spinner instead of empty body on initial modal open (#58)\n\n* fix(modal): show spinner instead of empty body on initial modal open\n\nAdd fallback branch in PluginDetailModal for the transitional state\nwhere pluginName is set but useEffect has not yet fired (loading=false,\nplugin=null, error=null). This eliminates a one-frame empty modal body.\n\nCloses #52\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use consistent pluginName fallback in modal header\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): use consistent deployment model formatting across pages (#59)\n\nMove deploymentModelLabel to shared utils and use it in CatalogPage\ncard footer, matching the formatted display already used in\nPluginDetailModal (e.g., ''Cluster-shared'' instead of ''cluster-shared'').\n\nCloses #54\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(modal): guard container image rendering against missing fields (#60)\n\nAdd runtime guards for image.repository before rendering and fall\nback to ''latest'' when image.tag is absent. Prevents displaying\n''repository:undefined'' from malformed BFF responses.\n\nCloses #55\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWjOGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA//EQAEDHpiw7/70KG6x8goERh0W8\neJ4UiFGNX/OvSvtk0Z3o7/1gCHdgHwg7S9iqNOyr+w82byIST0g1UpsaSqf/+HkE\naMvS7E752LcqjzF2NjOEgYKOfxyxmQvMuK3iGRB2BM3FUBHeqCjQwsmS7HFHM1vD\nN4jFGGojn3z9plTT5IPi2qupVVkfxiuKSeEXG20nna6T8SuyfVx+ZxOSrIFqtaVQ\njPzH134iTEy1ZOjJtO099cS4iY4Q7ZXRa6grAy7kTIR2aBbwOi3TGQ/1OxIv9jQd\n74u5dJHBohIo98Ykew6Jdq3F5X9SvTHdvb1PPDiLk8ySNmvHRQqeqrytyED8R5K8\nQkpsWTkPwk0aMjwnIHtQElitoe8YUqtNUOPNvXZy4bd1tjXg8cIA4fLQzc6SyF5i\nuaBfdZomeMzpK5BIha/NBshEj9u+D5T+2hYp6mCwkPUggeg4rdVwNE6ALm1F0EvU\n3LxMVpXad3lZ9qcuPMUJ1T5qj4cOJttha7jxivUVOvsj6CgV/B7xj9ZGHTiXwMz5\nXFhOb3550Lofe434UdFNW4S59HK5hwROxn/DoQLxR5m4UZK7Xf28F9VwT7U2+MZL\n4t/qNn9pFuWmgda89FB2XfZkyzzlgzeyZsBS2vxOMR9UHS2rKVXKct0Js3poQ6wh\nZ4p3wGkHRL4DrLy5fVOT\n=+ORP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T13:52:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.gith