m/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/4d6fcb646a735ada40ffd92b51556d5bc5ccdee6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T20:03:42Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T20:03:42Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"message":"feat: build catalog page with card grid, filters, and installed overlay\n\n- Add frontend CatalogPlugin types (src/app/types/catalog.ts)\n- Add useCatalog hook fetching from BFF /api/catalog with refetch\n- Add useInstalledPluginNames hook reading MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG\n- Rewrite CatalogPage with PatternFly card grid, toolbar with search\n  and multi-select filters (status, maintenance, install state)\n- Show Installed badge on cards for plugins in MODULE_FEDERATION_CONFIG\n- Wire PluginDetailModal to open on card click\n- Add unit tests for both hooks and the catalog page (25 new tests)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5d72b79a04e520833529116c194ff03439b6a0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/d5d72b79a04e520833529116c194ff03439b6a0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/4d6fcb646a735ada40ffd92b51556d5bc5ccdee6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/4d6fcb646a735ada40ffd92b51556d5bc5ccdee6","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKDRkNmZjYjY0NmE3MzVhZGE0MGZmZDkyYjUxNTU2ZDViYzVjY2RlZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/ca42c5ab326a0ead81f5c9563bde45a62103f4e2","sha":"ca42c5ab326a0ead81f5c9563bde45a62103f4e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/ca42c5ab326a0ead81f5c9563bde45a62103f4e2"}],"sha":"4d6fcb646a735ada40ffd92b51556d5bc5ccdee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/4d6fcb646a735ada40ffd92b51556d5bc5ccdee6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/ca42c5ab326a0ead81f5c9563bde45a62103f4e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T19:48:01Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T19:48:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 2 — BFF plugin metadata aggregation (#8)\n\n* feat: add BFF catalog endpoints with registry and metadata clients\n\nPhase 2 implementation: BFF plugin metadata aggregation.\n\n- Add charter registry client (charterClient.ts) that fetches plugins.yaml\n  from the charter GitHub repo with in-memory caching and stale-cache fallback\n- Add plugin metadata client (pluginMetadataClient.ts) that fetches individual\n  plugin.yaml files with per-plugin caching and concurrency limiting\n- Add catalog routes: GET /api/catalog (merged list) and GET /api/catalog/:name\n  (single plugin detail), with ?refresh=true cache invalidation\n- Define TypeScript types for registry entries, plugin metadata, and catalog response\n- Separate Express app from server startup (app.ts/server.ts split) for testability\n- Add js-yaml dependency for YAML parsing\n- Add comprehensive unit tests (28 new tests across 3 test files)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: extract shared fetchUrl into httpClient utility\n\nRemoves duplicated HTTP fetch logic from charterClient.ts and\npluginMetadataClient.ts into a shared utils/httpClient.ts module.\nUpdates tests to mock the shared module instead of https directly.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use consistent camelCase in catalog API response\n\nConvert snake_case fields from PluginInstall (chart_path) and\nPluginRbac (required_roles, cluster_roles) to camelCase in the\nCatalogPlugin response type. Ensures the JSON API is consistently\ncamelCase throughout while the internal PluginMetadata types still\nmatch the upstream YAML schema.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add unit tests for shared httpClient utility\n\nTests cover successful fetch, non-2xx status rejection, network error\nhandling, and redirect following.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update AGENTS.md to reflect Phase 2 BFF additions\n\nDocument new catalog endpoints, service clients, shared httpClient\nutility, and catalog types in the BFF Service section.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Add redirect depth limit (max 5) to prevent infinite redirect loops\n- Add 10s request timeout to prevent hanging on slow upstreams\n- Add 5MB response body size limit to prevent memory exhaustion\n- Strip .git suffix from repo URLs in buildRawUrl\n- Use RegistryPlugin type directly in buildCatalogPlugin parameter\n- Add tests for redirect limit and timeout behavior\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): preserve stale-cache fallback on refresh (#15)\n\nWhen ?refresh=true was passed, clearCharterCache() nulled the cache\nbefore getRegistryPlugins() attempted a fresh fetch. If the fetch\nfailed, the stale-cache fallback found cache===null and rethrew,\nreturning 502 even though valid data existed moments before.\n\nFix by adding a forceRefresh parameter to getRegistryPlugins(). When\ntrue, the function skips the TTL check but captures the current cache\nin a local staleCache variable before fetching. On failure the stale\ndata is returned as before. The route no longer calls clearCharterCache;\nit passes forceRefresh directly, keeping invalidation deferred until\na successful fetch updates the cache.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): drain response streams on redirect and error in httpClient (#16)\n\nAdd res.resume() before each early return in the redirect and error\nbranches of fetchUrl so the underlying TCP socket is released back to\nthe pool instead of remaining held open by an unconsumed IncomingMessage.\nCovers three paths: normal redirect follow, too-many-redirects rejection,\nand non-2xx status rejection.\n\nAdd three tests asserting resume() is called on each of those paths.\n\nFixes #10\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): support custom default branch in plugin metadata URL (#17)\n\nAdd optional `default_branch` field to `RegistryPlugin` type so registry maintainers can specify a non-main default branch. Update `buildRawUrl()` to use `plugin.default_branch ?? ''main''` instead of the hardcoded ''main'', preventing silent 404 failures for plugins whose default branch is ''master'' or any other name. Add tests covering master branch, absent field fallback, and arbitrary branch names.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): resolve relative Location headers in httpClient redirects (#18)\n\nResolve the Location header against the original request URL using\n`new URL(location, url).href` before recursing, so that relative\nredirect targets (e.g. `/new-path`) are correctly converted to\nabsolute URLs instead of being passed verbatim to https.get().\n\nAdds two tests covering root-relative and path-relative Location values.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(bff): use getPluginMetadata directly for single-plugin lookup (#19)\n\nThe GET /:name handler was calling getAllPluginMetadata([registryEntry]) —\nrunning the full batch concurrency machinery (runWithConcurrency worker\nsetup, results array, Map construction) for a single plugin. Switch to\ncalling getPluginMetadata(registryEntry) directly, which already handles\ncaching identically and returns the result without the batch overhead.\n\nUpdate catalogRoutes tests to mock getPluginMetadata instead of\ngetAllPluginMetadata for the single-plugin test cases.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): add aggregate failure detection to catalog endpoint (#20)\n\nWhen more than 50% of plugin metadata fetches fail (e.g., due to GitHub\nrate-limiting), the GET /api/catalog response now includes a warnings\narray with a human-readable message. HTTP status remains 200 so cached\nor partial results are still served; the warnings field lets consumers\ndetect the degraded state and surface it to operators.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"532efb572624cc472a686bbef4afab2613c69a83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/532efb572624cc472a686bbef4afab2613c69a83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/ca42c5ab326a0ead81f5c9563bde45a62103f4e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 532efb572624cc472a686bbef4afab2613c69a83\nparent d0ba2a7a553b779c6d2d62eb090cd4c8aed8e752\nparent c6560f54803e6ad0d933950aa1dba468a9fbbcbd\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784231281 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784231281 -0400\n\nfeat: Phase 2 — BFF plugin metadata aggregation (#8)\n\n* feat: add BFF catalog endpoints with registry and metadata clients\n\nPhase 2 implementation: BFF plugin metadata aggregation.\n\n- Add charter registry client (charterClient.ts) that fetches plugins.yaml\n  from the charter GitHub repo with in-memory caching and stale-cache fallback\n- Add plugin metadata client (pluginMetadataClient.ts) that fetches individual\n  plugin.yaml files with per-plugin caching and concurrency limiting\n- Add catalog routes: GET /api/catalog (merged list) and GET /api/catalog/:name\n  (single plugin detail), with ?refresh=true cache invalidation\n- Define TypeScript types for registry entries, plugin metadata, and catalog response\n- Separate Express app from server startup (app.ts/server.ts split) for testability\n- Add js-yaml dependency for YAML parsing\n- Add comprehensive unit tests (28 new tests across 3 test files)\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: extract shared fetchUrl into httpClient utility\n\nRemoves duplicated HTTP fetch logic from charterClient.ts and\npluginMetadataClient.ts into a shared utils/httpClient.ts module.\nUpdates tests to mock the shared module instead of https directly.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use consistent camelCase in catalog API response\n\nConvert snake_case fields from PluginInstall (chart_path) and\nPluginRbac (required_roles, cluster_roles) to camelCase in the\nCatalogPlugin response type. Ensures the JSON API is consistently\ncamelCase throughout while the internal PluginMetadata types still\nmatch the upstream YAML schema.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add unit tests for shared httpClient utility\n\nTests cover successful fetch, non-2xx status rejection, network error\nhandling, and redirect following.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update AGENTS.md to reflect Phase 2 BFF additions\n\nDocument new catalog endpoints, service clients, shared httpClient\nutility, and catalog types in the BFF Service section.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review findings (round 1)\n\n- Add redirect depth limit (max 5) to prevent infinite redirect loops\n- Add 10s request timeout to prevent hanging on slow upstreams\n- Add 5MB response body size limit to prevent memory exhaustion\n- Strip .git suffix from repo URLs in buildRawUrl\n- Use RegistryPlugin type directly in buildCatalogPlugin parameter\n- Add tests for redirect limit and timeout behavior\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): preserve stale-cache fallback on refresh (#15)\n\nWhen ?refresh=true was passed, clearCharterCache() nulled the cache\nbefore getRegistryPlugins() attempted a fresh fetch. If the fetch\nfailed, the stale-cache fallback found cache===null and rethrew,\nreturning 502 even though valid data existed moments before.\n\nFix by adding a forceRefresh parameter to getRegistryPlugins(). When\ntrue, the function skips the TTL check but captures the current cache\nin a local staleCache variable before fetching. On failure the stale\ndata is returned as before. The route no longer calls clearCharterCache;\nit passes forceRefresh directly, keeping invalidation deferred until\na successful fetch updates the cache.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): drain response streams on redirect and error in httpClient (#16)\n\nAdd res.resume() before each early return in the redirect and error\nbranches of fetchUrl so the underlying TCP socket is released back to\nthe pool instead of remaining held open by an unconsumed IncomingMessage.\nCovers three paths: normal redirect follow, too-many-redirects rejection,\nand non-2xx status rejection.\n\nAdd three tests asserting resume() is called on each of those paths.\n\nFixes #10\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): support custom default branch in plugin metadata URL (#17)\n\nAdd optional `default_branch` field to `RegistryPlugin` type so registry maintainers can specify a non-main default branch. Update `buildRawUrl()` to use `plugin.default_branch ?? ''main''` instead of the hardcoded ''main'', preventing silent 404 failures for plugins whose default branch is ''master'' or any other name. Add tests covering master branch, absent field fallback, and arbitrary branch names.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): resolve relative Location headers in httpClient redirects (#18)\n\nResolve the Location header against the original request URL using\n`new URL(location, url).href` before recursing, so that relative\nredirect targets (e.g. `/new-path`) are correctly converted to\nabsolute URLs instead of being passed verbatim to https.get().\n\nAdds two tests covering root-relative and path-relative Location values.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(bff): use getPluginMetadata directly for single-plugin lookup (#19)\n\nThe GET /:name handler was calling getAllPluginMetadata([registryEntry]) —\nrunning the full batch concurrency machinery (runWithConcurrency worker\nsetup, results array, Map construction) for a single plugin. Switch to\ncalling getPluginMetadata(registryEntry) directly, which already handles\ncaching identically and returns the result without the batch overhead.\n\nUpdate catalogRoutes tests to mock getPluginMetadata instead of\ngetAllPluginMetadata for the single-plugin test cases.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bff): add aggregate failure detection to catalog endpoint (#20)\n\nWhen more than 50% of plugin metadata fetches fail (e.g., due to GitHub\nrate-limiting), the GET /api/catalog response now includes a warnings\narray with a human-readable message. HTTP status remains 200 so cached\nor partial results are still served; the warnings field lets consumers\ndetect the degraded state and surface it to operators.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWTVxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATtMQAFbeyDjWw4yr67g0FFaY/wwF\nSlt2SsVYKP3PHmvzCmFVS+ksvWK8Vc1qA9utND6WhsGiZXbg63jLcl/nhG1NnCl+\n//L6xSsFszUd5jSVWGTK863WO29QzYuYAQW61Q9hrTKLGSUEaAGqeGndkDi5iBly\nZFHqrQgPHDiU3NAjbqAlPPqN2hAiubng4WHdPB7vbr/JT0FWQHRAfcE6O4V3ugOA\nYZpvHJ6XqukbjzAaSmxQaNyUBdhYEh4GAvp7ofQku8D15TxBOcTJqbaiRiSHHLO/\nunAVA1CdJYHFNoPuxhfm2WZolwXNmKKT/zaxLynh2FguGUCZa6melNOOvH0H/o1d\nczvzuHR5ka2tsT1yCLh2sbm2m7A693vpqxlgovOVzj34q1m+x8fDEZxaRnZxdhEG\nQ6xXpmckhBYgEXEIT+HiBPkZpygGpn+nDBeZnLti1tgENT01Ck8zCtJqByr+Qcvu\nECpKbKDczRGgYMeHfi2oZFlen10Z3Bvkl8jk76NwXX7k/9mJX3p0uvgVOynUwdOA\nLalczEHvjEdR6Au2zfPNxF4qta9yfE1g91xBAHMypc7IkvPwXKGEULYGRLXHgqZK\n