","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/325992a11f748d4c5fd589c3f551569522f20644/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T19:17:59Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T19:17:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): resolve relative Location headers in httpClient redirects (#18)\n\nResolve the Location header against the original request URL using\n`new URL(location, url).href` before recursing, so that relative\nredirect targets (e.g. `/new-path`) are correctly converted to\nabsolute URLs instead of being passed verbatim to https.get().\n\nAdds two tests covering root-relative and path-relative Location values.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78ba20b90a60cc1e04d2e282e8eb9964b5b0dd44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/78ba20b90a60cc1e04d2e282e8eb9964b5b0dd44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/325992a11f748d4c5fd589c3f551569522f20644","verification":{"payload":"tree 78ba20b90a60cc1e04d2e282e8eb9964b5b0dd44\nparent ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784229479 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784229479 -0400\n\nfix(bff): resolve relative Location headers in httpClient redirects (#18)\n\nResolve the Location header against the original request URL using\n`new URL(location, url).href` before recursing, so that relative\nredirect targets (e.g. `/new-path`) are correctly converted to\nabsolute URLs instead of being passed verbatim to https.get().\n\nAdds two tests covering root-relative and path-relative Location values.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWS5nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN1QQAJiUu5SeGv70eTohZdHaAwLu\nSmKvEJ1ilIfX2ERbgWCfjXjvbvLniV+6sQTrB3cqnOt+jZumzchBQHfcgVor4qsE\nbX30KdAm3dPzBIvTMBYkH6qAGX72fJQ9Zfgm88PIAB4Y83DNXtE1colk2/LVjibS\nVM0rzLCCCUG54KGf18nw+PJbqGNOYBi0DbQTjrw0YdlphHWhIGe8hnMYosPJIjJZ\nWBR6dw2TlfUathmbBsS1TRoarcRK6NgojYNgz5zrpK8nOx2NhSaoDuy/ab4T9dRH\nOQA7iwwWrLveaLzULdvza64gD7Apj4LaWFtqUpZOUlLFKKsosll+l0Xkw7mIr/BD\nWHIUSSCmCbbW5pdv0o9kGn5OCAvicfQVFyOu3dweE764JkbCc22JQVdyNuqCP72D\njaQQ7CnxriV6pDehtbvQE4NGKo8Oc2MkGVF7lWQVp8TsMDb6ASGu6Jw4/jlnf+/j\nBNLPvWRvz783JiXA2DfkM2lvIOv5L2VmC+w3yMJMm4MY+zltC7Dg2BQ1lwmiuq0F\n9Tkt1RJqpgENrjip1KsRP4gtJ4rbnH8pU7++5xffMyPliu3ZtlGqI4XYIhypaScV\nGqyZVZRgh2s3+tnxEhicH1iBOiKdfEPSPMDPPTs0BHifbYnx8ngg97LiVKu10Feq\njjNYgiKhOLwOCZfltoAc\n=PH8E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T19:18:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/325992a11f748d4c5fd589c3f551569522f20644","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKDMyNTk5MmExMWY3NDhkNGM1ZmQ1ODljM2Y1NTE1Njk1MjJmMjA2NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e","sha":"ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e"}],"sha":"325992a11f748d4c5fd589c3f551569522f20644","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/325992a11f748d4c5fd589c3f551569522f20644"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T19:13:59Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T19:13:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): support custom default branch in plugin metadata URL (#17)\n\nAdd optional `default_branch` field to `RegistryPlugin` type so registry maintainers can specify a non-main default branch. Update `buildRawUrl()` to use `plugin.default_branch ?? ''main''` instead of the hardcoded ''main'', preventing silent 404 failures for plugins whose default branch is ''master'' or any other name. Add tests covering master branch, absent field fallback, and arbitrary branch names.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f554042892c49e779cf11d3a8fbe982308a56ada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/f554042892c49e779cf11d3a8fbe982308a56ada"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e","verification":{"payload":"tree f554042892c49e779cf11d3a8fbe982308a56ada\nparent dceeaecbadc0c50c45c7fdf8cff76d6c4c36a061\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784229239 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784229239 -0400\n\nfix(bff): support custom default branch in plugin metadata URL (#17)\n\nAdd optional `default_branch` field to `RegistryPlugin` type so registry maintainers can specify a non-main default branch. Update `buildRawUrl()` to use `plugin.default_branch ?? ''main''` instead of the hardcoded ''main'', preventing silent 404 failures for plugins whose default branch is ''master'' or any other name. Add tests covering master branch, absent field fallback, and arbitrary branch names.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWS13CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXPgQAATHbdUBnY8eoT5YwAyWUArK\n2eOKI41mKAUKkEwKXFVVg8ZncA81fHbrIOYIIP8q7Q++Io+Oogh1tqZtD/NYQ+d7\nbuFA+H30LW+rBv4588QWiWdXAj2Au0439bUWkQIhqBT6A/kKnTJDcadUovHjLdMt\nl1MqbE74/4FiUgXp5A8UEt//hSnZSHXdzZ+a/GgLw6jwiAZkYGzOpTsXhk4daEsD\n1FuoZ4fCTvWIgBVzpMjsnRjY7IPZuIAbtcO0b7hOcBt+YZNcySE7m1l+ivDCmqx8\nnayJywAbouOGFupjW0G+ZYdahBcIisxw7VXu70yblTA5vn/zqIXx8x5blTtOXdd5\nc6cwD18m06yIRMfZO5p1UAMzlOoz4X7OTc46ma6lZYZgt39f3VKGalcAO6LfbOJi\nhsSrNDjdyHS5CpPGG+NVmzQyW/9QKcQRWLUzU/tWlETjuKxSOYBNbJ6CGGBWyhzN\nNEl1C8Z6YaAPuoch1rR6sFR9ddpGUf5jLPfkv36yAL+PyitB6puuxVc9REkcL6hP\ncAOQ0ukQHLQsx8KyDE+JryzGpNbU6ffbbW00axnBwWusWp3/I8FmIGjSt53IRdtL\nmlwo1Plm8o9sWeLi6l5B7lPeLkBkxp0PmOeGqVRb/SA6+eIrt8JTxc8SCk7WkrvQ\nta93rJlLGd2+4Fv9NktE\n=TpQ4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T19:14:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e","node_id":"C_kwDOTaij69oAKGJhNGY0MTQ0YWY5NTY3MzgzMzBjNWM3NDgyYjM4OWM4Yzc0NTVkMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commit/dceeaecbadc0c50c45c7fdf8cff76d6c4c36a061","sha":"dceeaecbadc0c50c45c7fdf8cff76d6c4c36a061","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/dceeaecbadc0c50c45c7fdf8cff76d6c4c36a061"}],"sha":"ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/ba4f4144af956738330c5c7482b389c8c7455d0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/commits/dceeaecbadc0c50c45c7fdf8cff76d6c4c36a061/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T19:13:56Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T19:13:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bff): drain response streams on redirect and error in httpClient (#16)\n\nAdd res.resume() before each early return in the redirect and error\nbranches of fetchUrl so the underlying TCP socket is released back to\nthe pool instead of remaining held open by an unconsumed IncomingMessage.\nCovers three paths: normal redirect follow, too-many-redirects rejection,\nand non-2xx status rejection.\n\nAdd three tests asserting resume() is called on each of those paths.\n\nFixes #10\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"667da1be32d33360d1acf2a891adf8b569360731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/trees/667da1be32d33360d1acf2a891adf8b569360731"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/community-plugins-admin/git/commits/dceeaecbadc0c50c45c7fdf8cff76d6c4c36a061","verification":{"payload":"tree 667da1be32d33360d1acf2a891adf8b569360731\nparent 88be38ed2d0387c087e3bb8d736bfc1bac3783da\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1784229236 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784229236 -0400\n\nfix(bff): drain response streams on redirect and error in httpClient (#16)\n\nAdd res.resume() before each early return in the redirect and error\nbranches of fetchUrl so the underlying TCP socket is released back to\nthe pool instead of remaining held open by an unconsumed IncomingMessage.\nCovers three paths: normal redirect follow, too-many-redirects rejection,\nand non-2xx status rejection.\n\nAdd three tests asserting resume() is called on each of those paths.\n\nFixes #10\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWS10CRC1aQ7uu5UhlA